window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-15-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-15-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 15 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000073881","section":"REASONING","topic":"Clock & Calendar","question":{"en":"The Chennai seminar was on 4th July, and the Guwahati on 10th July. The Ahmedabad seminar happened on a date divisible by 4 between them. Pick the CORRECT date. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"चेन्नई का सेमिनार 4 जुलाई को और गुवाहाटी का 10 जुलाई को था। अहमदाबाद का सेमिनार इनके बीच की उस तारीख को हुआ जो 4 से विभाज्य है। सही तारीख चुनिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5th July","hi":"5 जुलाई"},"2":{"en":"6th July","hi":"6 जुलाई"},"3":{"en":"7th July","hi":"7 जुलाई"},"4":{"en":"8th July","hi":"8 जुलाई"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The dates between 4th and 10th July are 5, 6, 7, 8 and 9<br>The date divisible by 4 among them is 8<br>So the Ahmedabad seminar was on 8th July<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8th July.</b>","hi":"4 और 10 जुलाई के बीच की तारीखें 5, 6, 7, 8 तथा 9 हैं<br>इनमें 4 से विभाज्य तारीख 8 है<br>अतः अहमदाबाद का सेमिनार 8 जुलाई को था<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8 जुलाई है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000073882","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If A = 2, B = 4, C = 6, then E = ? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि A = 2, B = 4, C = 6 है, तो E = ? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8"},"2":{"en":"10"},"3":{"en":"12"},"4":{"en":"14"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Each letter is replaced by double its alphabet position: A = 1 × 2 = 2, B = 2 × 2 = 4, C = 3 × 2 = 6<br>E is the 5th letter, so E = 5 × 2 = 10<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 10.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर को उसके वर्णमाला स्थान का दोगुना मान दिया गया है: A = 1 × 2 = 2, B = 2 × 2 = 4, C = 3 × 2 = 6<br>E पाँचवाँ अक्षर है, अतः E = 5 × 2 = 10<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 10 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000073883","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"In a certain code, 541X1082 is a valid roll number. What is the rule? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी निश्चित कूट में 541X1082 एक वैध रोल नंबर है। नियम क्या है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Second number is twice the first","hi":"दूसरी संख्या पहली की दोगुनी है"},"2":{"en":"Second number is double first minus 1","hi":"दूसरी संख्या पहली की दोगुनी में से 1 घटाकर है"},"3":{"en":"Second number is double first plus 1","hi":"दूसरी संख्या पहली की दोगुनी में 1 जोड़कर है"},"4":{"en":"Second number is first number squared","hi":"दूसरी संख्या पहली संख्या का वर्ग है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The two numbers in the roll number are 541 and 1082<br>541 × 2 = 1082, which shows that the second number is exactly twice the first<br>So the rule is that the second number is twice the first<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Second number is twice the first.</b>","hi":"रोल नंबर की दो संख्याएँ 541 और 1082 हैं<br>541 × 2 = 1082, जिससे स्पष्ट है कि दूसरी संख्या पहली की ठीक दोगुनी है<br>अतः नियम यह है कि दूसरी संख्या पहली की दोगुनी है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): दूसरी संख्या पहली की दोगुनी है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000073884","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The HCF of two numbers is 12 and their LCM is 180. If one number is 60, what is the other? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो संख्याओं का म.स.प. 12 और ल.स.प. 180 है। यदि एक संख्या 60 है, तो दूसरी संख्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"36"},"2":{"en":"24"},"3":{"en":"40"},"4":{"en":"90"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"For two numbers, first × second = HCF × LCM<br>60 × second = 12 × 180 = 2160<br>Second number = \\(\\frac{2160}{60}=36\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 36.</b>","hi":"दो संख्याओं के लिए, पहली × दूसरी = म.स.प. × ल.स.प.<br>60 × दूसरी = 12 × 180 = 2160<br>दूसरी संख्या = \\(\\frac{2160}{60}=36\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 36 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000073885","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A shopkeeper marked an item 25% above cost price and allowed a discount of 10%. What is his profit percentage? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक दुकानदार ने वस्तु पर लागत मूल्य से 25% अधिक अंकित मूल्य लगाया और 10% की छूट दी। उसका लाभ प्रतिशत क्या है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15%"},"2":{"en":"10%"},"3":{"en":"20%"},"4":{"en":"12.5%"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let the cost price be 100, then the marked price = 125<br>Selling price = 125 × 0.90 = 112.5<br>Profit = 112.5 − 100 = 12.5, so profit percentage = 12.5%<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 12.5%.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए लागत मूल्य 100 है, तो अंकित मूल्य = 125<br>विक्रय मूल्य = 125 × 0.90 = 112.5<br>लाभ = 112.5 − 100 = 12.5, अतः लाभ प्रतिशत = 12.5%<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 12.5% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000073886","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What comes next?<br>5, 17, 37, 65, 101, ? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"अगला पद क्या आएगा?<br>5, 17, 37, 65, 101, ? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"145"},"2":{"en":"139"},"3":{"en":"137"},"4":{"en":"130"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Differences are 12, 20, 28, 36, which rise by 8 each time<br>Next difference = 44, so next term = 101 + 44 = 145<br>The terms also fit (2n)² + 1 for n = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, giving 145 for n = 6<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 145.</b>","hi":"अंतर 12, 20, 28, 36 हैं, जो हर बार 8 से बढ़ते हैं<br>अगला अंतर = 44, अतः अगला पद = 101 + 44 = 145<br>पद (2n)² + 1 से भी मेल खाते हैं जहाँ n = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 है और n = 6 के लिए 145 मिलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 145 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000073887","section":"REASONING","topic":"Seating & Mixed Arrangement","question":{"en":"Read the following information carefully and answer the question given below.<br>Nine different colour boxes, viz, Red, Black, Pink, Blue, White, Orange, Green, Yellow and Brown are placed one above the other but not necessarily in the same order. Five boxes are placed between the Red and Blue box. The Orange colour box is placed immediately above the Blue box. Only three boxes are between the Orange colour box and the White box. As many boxes are placed between Red and White as between Black and Orange. The Green colour box is placed below the Black box but not at the bottom. More than four boxes are placed between Orange and Green. One box is between Green and Yellow. The Pink box is placed above the Brown box.<br>Which of the following statements is FALSE regarding the White colour box? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित जानकारी ध्यान से पढ़िए और नीचे दिए प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br>नौ भिन्न रंगों के डिब्बे, अर्थात् Red, Black, Pink, Blue, White, Orange, Green, Yellow और Brown एक-दूसरे के ऊपर रखे गए हैं, परंतु आवश्यक नहीं कि इसी क्रम में हों। Red और Blue डिब्बे के बीच पाँच डिब्बे हैं। Orange रंग का डिब्बा Blue डिब्बे के ठीक ऊपर है। Orange रंग के डिब्बे और White डिब्बे के बीच केवल तीन डिब्बे हैं। Red और White के बीच जितने डिब्बे हैं, उतने ही Black और Orange के बीच हैं। Green रंग का डिब्बा Black डिब्बे के नीचे है परंतु सबसे नीचे नहीं है। Orange और Green के बीच चार से अधिक डिब्बे हैं। Green और Yellow के बीच एक डिब्बा है। Pink डिब्बा Brown डिब्बे के ऊपर है।<br>White रंग के डिब्बे के बारे में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन असत्य है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only one box is placed between the White box and Pink box.","hi":"White और Pink डिब्बे के बीच केवल एक डिब्बा है।"},"2":{"en":"Blue box is placed below White box.","hi":"Blue डिब्बा White डिब्बे के नीचे है।"},"3":{"en":"Brown box is immediately below the White box.","hi":"Brown डिब्बा White डिब्बे के ठीक नीचे है।"},"4":{"en":"White colour box is placed exactly in the middle.","hi":"White रंग का डिब्बा ठीक मध्य में है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Final arrangement (top to bottom): Orange, Blue, Pink, Black, White, Brown, Green, Red, Yellow<br><svg width=\"164\" height=\"250\" viewBox=\"0 0 164 250\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><rect x=\"44\" y=\"22\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"46\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"70\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"94\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"118\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#fff3c4\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"142\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"166\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"190\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"214\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"27\" y=\"16\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">Box</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">1</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"38\">Orange</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">2</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"62\">Blue</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">3</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"86\">Pink</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">4</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"110\">Black</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">5</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"134\">White</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">6</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"158\">Brown</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">7</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"182\">Green</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">8</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"206\">Red</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">9</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"230\">Yellow</text></g></svg><br>White is 5th (exactly in the middle), Brown is just below it, one box (Black) is between White and Pink, and Blue is above White.<br>So 'Blue box is placed below White box' is false.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Blue box is placed below White box..</b>","hi":"अंतिम व्यवस्था (ऊपर से नीचे): नारंगी, नीला, गुलाबी, काला, सफ़ेद, भूरा, हरा, लाल, पीला<br><svg width=\"164\" height=\"250\" viewBox=\"0 0 164 250\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><rect x=\"44\" y=\"22\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"46\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"70\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"94\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"118\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#fff3c4\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"142\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"166\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"190\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"214\" width=\"110\" height=\"24\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"27\" y=\"16\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\">Box</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">1</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"38\">Orange</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">2</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"62\">Blue</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">3</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"86\">Pink</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">4</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"110\">Black</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">5</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"134\">White</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">6</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"158\">Brown</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">7</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"182\">Green</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">8</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"206\">Red</text><text x=\"27\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#555\">9</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"230\">Yellow</text></g></svg><br>सफ़ेद पाँचवाँ (ठीक मध्य में) है, भूरा ठीक उसके नीचे है, सफ़ेद और गुलाबी के बीच एक डिब्बा (काला) है तथा नीला सफ़ेद के ऊपर है।<br>अतः 'नीला डिब्बा सफ़ेद डिब्बे के नीचे रखा है' असत्य है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): Blue डिब्बा White डिब्बे के नीचे है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000073888","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"Find the group of letters that best completes the analogy. Use alphabetical positions and reverse position logic where necessary.<br>ADMS : ZWNH :: BCFK : ? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"अक्षरों का वह समूह ज्ञात कीजिए जो सादृश्य को सर्वोत्तम रूप से पूरा करता है। आवश्यकतानुसार वर्णमाला स्थान तथा विपरीत स्थान का तर्क प्रयोग कीजिए।<br>ADMS : ZWNH :: BCFK : ? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"YXUP"},"2":{"en":"YXUL"},"3":{"en":"YXTP"},"4":{"en":"YXTL"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Every letter is replaced by the letter at the same distance from the other end of the alphabet: A→Z, D→W, M→N, S→H, i.e. position n becomes 27 − n<br>BCFK gives B→Y, C→X, F→U, K→P<br>So the answer is YXUP<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): YXUP.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर को वर्णमाला के दूसरे सिरे से समान दूरी वाले अक्षर से बदला जाता है: A→Z, D→W, M→N, S→H, अर्थात स्थान n, 27 − n बन जाता है<br>BCFK से B→Y, C→X, F→U, K→P<br>अतः उत्तर YXUP है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): YXUP है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000073889","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the questions given below, there are three statements followed by three conclusions I, II, and III. You have to take the given three statements to be true, even if they seem to be at variance from commonly known facts.<br>Read all the conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusions logically follows from the given statements, disregarding commonly known facts.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>Some Drain are Leakage<br>All Leakage are Hole<br>No Leakage are Dump<br><b>Conclusion:</b><br>I. No Hole are Dump<br>II. Some Hole can be Dump<br>III. Some Drain are Hole [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"नीचे दिए प्रश्नों में तीन कथन और उनके बाद तीन निष्कर्ष I, II तथा III दिए गए हैं। दिए गए तीनों कथनों को सत्य मानना है, भले ही वे सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न प्रतीत हों।<br>सभी निष्कर्षों को पढ़िए और फिर निर्णय कीजिए कि सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों को छोड़कर कौन-सा निष्कर्ष दिए गए कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कुछ Drain, Leakage हैं<br>सभी Leakage, Hole हैं<br>कोई Leakage, Dump नहीं है<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. कोई Hole, Dump नहीं है<br>II. कुछ Hole, Dump हो सकते हैं<br>III. कुछ Drain, Hole हैं [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I अनुसरण करता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusions I and II follow","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I और II अनुसरण करते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only conclusions II and III follow","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II और III अनुसरण करते हैं"},"4":{"en":"All the conclusions follow","hi":"सभी निष्कर्ष अनुसरण करते हैं"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Since no Leakage is a Dump and all Leakage are Hole, only the Leakage part of Hole is surely away from Dump, so 'No Hole are Dump' is not certain and I does not follow<br>The remaining part of Hole may be inside Dump, so II follows as a possibility<br>Some Drain are Leakage and all Leakage are Hole, so some Drain are Hole; III follows<br>Hence only conclusions II and III follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only conclusions II and III follow.</b>","hi":"चूँकि कोई Leakage, Dump नहीं है और सभी Leakage, Hole हैं, केवल Hole का Leakage वाला भाग ही निश्चित रूप से Dump से दूर है, अतः 'कोई Hole, Dump नहीं है' निश्चित नहीं और I अनुसरण नहीं करता<br>Hole का शेष भाग Dump के भीतर हो सकता है, अतः II संभावना के रूप में अनुसरण करता है<br>कुछ Drain, Leakage हैं और सभी Leakage, Hole हैं, अतः कुछ Drain, Hole हैं; III अनुसरण करता है<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष II और III अनुसरण करते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल निष्कर्ष II और III अनुसरण करते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000073890","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code, OBJECT is written as OTBJEC. How is MARKET written? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी निश्चित कूट में OBJECT को OTBJEC लिखा जाता है। MARKET को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"MTARKE"},"2":{"en":"MERKAT"},"3":{"en":"MREKAT"},"4":{"en":"MTAKRE"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The first letter stays in its place and the last letter is brought to the second place, all others shifting one place right: O BJ EC T → O T BJ EC<br>MARKET gives M T A R K E<br>Code = MTARKE<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): MTARKE.</b>","hi":"पहला अक्षर अपने स्थान पर रहता है और अंतिम अक्षर दूसरे स्थान पर आ जाता है, शेष सभी एक स्थान दाएँ खिसकते हैं: O BJ EC T → O T BJ EC<br>MARKET से M T A R K E<br>कूट = MTARKE<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): MTARKE है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000073891","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If PLANE is coded as QMBOF, how is QMBOF coded? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि PLANE को QMBOF कूट किया जाता है, तो QMBOF को कैसे कूट किया जाएगा? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RNCPG"},"2":{"en":"PLNED"},"3":{"en":"RMCPG"},"4":{"en":"QMBNF"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Every letter moves one step forward: P→Q, L→M, A→B, N→O, E→F<br>Applying the same step to QMBOF gives R N C P G<br>Code = RNCPG<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): RNCPG.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर एक कदम आगे बढ़ता है: P→Q, L→M, A→B, N→O, E→F<br>यही कदम QMBOF पर लगाने से R N C P G मिलता है<br>कूट = RNCPG<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): RNCPG है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000073892","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"CHARACTERISTIC\" is written as \"CIASADTFRJSUID\". How will \"ADMINISTRATION\" be written? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"CHARACTERISTIC\" को \"CIASADTFRJSUID\" लिखा जाता है। \"ADMINISTRATION\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"AEMJNSRUJBTJOO"},"2":{"en":"AEMJNJSURJBOTO"},"3":{"en":"AEMJNSJURBTJOO"},"4":{"en":"AEMJNJSURBTJOO"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Letters at odd places stay the same and letters at even places move one step ahead: CHARACTERISTIC → CIASADTFRJSUID<br>ADMINISTRATION: A, D→E, M, I→J, N, I→J, S, T→U, R, A→B, T, I→J, O, N→O<br>Code = AEMJNJSURBTJOO<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): AEMJNJSURBTJOO.</b>","hi":"विषम स्थानों के अक्षर वैसे ही रहते हैं और सम स्थानों के अक्षर एक स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं: CHARACTERISTIC → CIASADTFRJSUID<br>ADMINISTRATION: A, D→E, M, I→J, N, I→J, S, T→U, R, A→B, T, I→J, O, N→O<br>कूट = AEMJNJSURBTJOO<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): AEMJNJSURBTJOO है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000073893","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Find the missing number in the following series:<br>61, 211, ?, 991, 1717 [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित श्रेणी में लुप्त संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए:<br>61, 211, ?, 991, 1717 [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"505"},"2":{"en":"515"},"3":{"en":"525"},"4":{"en":"545"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The terms are cubes of 4, 6, 8, 10, 12 minus the odd numbers 3, 5, 7, 9, 11:<br>4³ − 3 = 61, 6³ − 5 = 211, 8³ − 7 = 505, 10³ − 9 = 991, 12³ − 11 = 1717<br>So the missing term = 8³ − 7 = 512 − 7 = 505<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 505.</b>","hi":"पद 4, 6, 8, 10, 12 के घन में से विषम संख्याएँ 3, 5, 7, 9, 11 घटाकर बनते हैं:<br>4³ − 3 = 61, 6³ − 5 = 211, 8³ − 7 = 505, 10³ − 9 = 991, 12³ − 11 = 1717<br>अतः लुप्त पद = 8³ − 7 = 512 − 7 = 505<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 505 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000073894","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"How many such S are there which are immediately preceded by T and immediately followed by Q?<br><b>Sequence:</b><br>TSQTSQTSSQTQ [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"ऐसे कितने S हैं जिनके ठीक पहले T और ठीक बाद Q आता है?<br><b>क्रम:</b><br>TSQTSQTSSQTQ [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Marking the letters: T S Q T S Q T S S Q T Q<br>The S at the second place has T before it and Q after it ✔<br>The S at the fifth place also has T before it and Q after it ✔; the next two S are not followed by Q<br>So there are 2 such S<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2.</b>","hi":"अक्षरों को अंकित करने पर: T S Q T S Q T S S Q T Q<br>दूसरे स्थान का S, जिससे पहले T और बाद में Q है ✔<br>पाँचवें स्थान का S भी, जिससे पहले T और बाद में Q है ✔; अगले दो S के बाद Q नहीं है<br>अतः ऐसे 2 S हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000073895","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"P has three children. Q is R's brother, and R is S's sister. T, the wife of P, is S's mother. There is only one daughter of P. What is the relation of S with Q? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"P के तीन संतान हैं। Q, R का भाई है और R, S की बहन है। P की पत्नी T, S की माता है। P की केवल एक पुत्री है। S का Q से क्या संबंध है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Paternal Uncle","hi":"चाचा"},"2":{"en":"Brother","hi":"भाई"},"3":{"en":"Nephew","hi":"भतीजा"},"4":{"en":"Cousin","hi":"चचेरा भाई"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"108\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 108\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"84\" y=\"62\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"182\" y=\"62\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M135 14H157M135 18H157M146 18V50M98 50H195M98 50V62M146 50V62M195 50V62\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"22\">P+</text><text x=\"173\" y=\"22\">T−</text><text x=\"98\" y=\"76\">Q+</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"76\">R−</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"76\">S+</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"103\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>P's only daughter is R, so the third child S is a son and Q's brother.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Brother.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"108\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 108\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"84\" y=\"62\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"182\" y=\"62\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M135 14H157M135 18H157M146 18V50M98 50H195M98 50V62M146 50V62M195 50V62\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"22\">P+</text><text x=\"173\" y=\"22\">T−</text><text x=\"98\" y=\"76\">Q+</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"76\">R−</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"76\">S+</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"103\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>P की इकलौती पुत्री R है, अतः तीसरी संतान S पुत्र है और Q का भाई है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): भाई है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000073896","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of characters is given. These characters follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing character accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">23</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में अक्षरों/संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करते हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त अक्षर/संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">23</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"43"},"2":{"en":"59"},"3":{"en":"65"},"4":{"en":"71"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In each row the third number is the product of the first two minus their sum<br>7 × 3 − (7 + 3) = 21 − 10 = 11 ✔ and 4 × 9 − (4 + 9) = 36 − 13 = 23 ✔<br>Missing number = 11 × 7 − (11 + 7) = 77 − 18 = 59<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 59.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पंक्ति में तीसरी संख्या पहली दो संख्याओं के गुणनफल में से उनका योग घटाकर मिलती है<br>7 × 3 − (7 + 3) = 21 − 10 = 11 ✔ तथा 4 × 9 − (4 + 9) = 36 − 13 = 23 ✔<br>लुप्त संख्या = 11 × 7 − (11 + 7) = 77 − 18 = 59<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 59 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000073897","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"A meaningful word starting with A is formed using the 2nd, 3rd, 4th and 7th letters of the word HARMONY. Which is the second letter of the new word formed? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"HARMONY शब्द के दूसरे, तीसरे, चौथे और सातवें अक्षरों से A से शुरू होने वाला एक अर्थपूर्ण शब्द बनाया जाता है। बने नए शब्द का दूसरा अक्षर कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"R"},"2":{"en":"M"},"3":{"en":"A"},"4":{"en":"Y"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"HARMONY: 2nd = A, 3rd = R, 4th = M, 7th = Y, so the letters are A, R, M, Y<br>The meaningful word starting with A is ARMY<br>Its second letter is R<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): R.</b>","hi":"HARMONY: दूसरा = A, तीसरा = R, चौथा = M, सातवाँ = Y, अतः अक्षर हैं A, R, M, Y<br>A से शुरू होने वाला अर्थपूर्ण शब्द ARMY है<br>इसका दूसरा अक्षर R है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): R है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000073898","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Select the odd number pair from the given alternatives. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए विकल्पों में से विषम संख्या युग्म चुनिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8, 512"},"2":{"en":"11, 1331"},"3":{"en":"13, 2197"},"4":{"en":"15, 3380"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"8³ = 512 ✔, 11³ = 1331 ✔ and 13³ = 2197 ✔, so in these pairs the second number is the cube of the first<br>15³ = 3375, not 3380 ✘<br>So 15, 3380 is the odd pair<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 15, 3380.</b>","hi":"8³ = 512 ✔, 11³ = 1331 ✔ तथा 13³ = 2197 ✔, अतः इन युग्मों में दूसरी संख्या पहली का घन है<br>15³ = 3375 है, 3380 नहीं ✘<br>अतः 15, 3380 विषम युग्म है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 15, 3380 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000073899","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You have arranged a dance party at your apartment for a Diwali celebration. At 10:30 PM, a neighbour requests that you switch off the loudspeakers due to the late hour. What is the most responsible and neighbourly action to take in this situation? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आपने दीवाली के उत्सव के लिए अपने अपार्टमेंट में डांस पार्टी आयोजित की है। रात 10:30 बजे एक पड़ोसी देर हो जाने के कारण लाउडस्पीकर बंद करने का अनुरोध करता है। इस स्थिति में सबसे उत्तरदायी और पड़ोसी-हितैषी कार्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Politely ask the neighbor to adjust their expectations and tolerate the noise, arguing that the Diwali festival occurs only once per year.","hi":"विनम्रता से पड़ोसी से कहें कि वे अपनी अपेक्षाएँ बदलें और शोर सहन करें, यह तर्क देते हुए कि दीवाली वर्ष में केवल एक बार आती है।"},"2":{"en":"Switch the loudspeakers off temporarily to appease the neighbor, but secretly turn them back on again immediately after the neighbor leaves your vicinity.","hi":"पड़ोसी को संतुष्ट करने के लिए लाउडस्पीकर कुछ समय बंद करें, परंतु पड़ोसी के जाते ही चुपचाप फिर चालू कर दें।"},"3":{"en":"Along with your gathered friends, aggressively threaten to physically intimidate the neighbor if they do not leave your apartment area immediately.","hi":"अपने साथियों के साथ पड़ोसी को तुरंत परिसर छोड़ने के लिए शारीरिक रूप से डराने की धमकी दें।"},"4":{"en":"Immediately switch off the loudspeakers to respect local noise regulations and sincerely apologize to the neighbor for the unintended inconvenience caused.","hi":"स्थानीय ध्वनि नियमों का सम्मान करते हुए लाउडस्पीकर तुरंत बंद कर दें और हुई असुविधा के लिए पड़ोसी से हृदय से क्षमा माँगें।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Late-night loud music disturbs others and violates local noise rules, so the neighbour's request is reasonable<br>Switching off the speakers at once and apologising keeps the festival spirit without harming anyone<br>Insisting, cheating or threatening turns a small matter into a conflict<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Immediately switch off the loudspeakers to respect local noise regulations and sincerely apologize to the neighbor for the unintended inconvenience caused.</b>","hi":"देर रात तेज़ संगीत दूसरों को परेशान करता है और स्थानीय ध्वनि नियमों का उल्लंघन है, अतः पड़ोसी का अनुरोध उचित है<br>तुरंत लाउडस्पीकर बंद करके क्षमा माँगना उत्सव की भावना बनाए रखता है और किसी को हानि नहीं पहुँचाता<br>ज़िद करना, धोखा देना या धमकाना छोटी बात को टकराव बना देता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): स्थानीय ध्वनि नियमों का सम्मान करते हुए लाउडस्पीकर तुरंत बंद कर दें और हुई असुविधा के लिए पड़ोसी से हृदय से क्षमा माँगें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000073900","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You are an auditor. You discover that the branch manager, who is also the person who mentored you into your current senior role, has been slightly inflating travel reimbursement claims for three years. The total amount is small, but it is a clear violation of company policy. The manager is currently the favourite to become the next Chief Operating Officer, a role that would be a huge benefit to your entire department. What is the most emotionally intelligent path for you to take? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आप एक अंकेक्षक (ऑडिटर) हैं। आप पाते हैं कि शाखा प्रबंधक, जो आपको आपके वर्तमान वरिष्ठ पद तक पहुँचाने में मार्गदर्शक रहा है, तीन वर्ष से यात्रा प्रतिपूर्ति के दावों में थोड़ी वृद्धि कर रहा है। राशि कम है, परंतु यह कंपनी नीति का स्पष्ट उल्लंघन है। प्रबंधक इस समय अगले मुख्य परिचालन अधिकारी बनने का प्रबल दावेदार है, जो पद आपके पूरे विभाग के लिए बहुत लाभकारी होगा। आपके लिए सबसे भावनात्मक रूप से बुद्धिमान मार्ग क्या है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ignore the findings to safeguard your mentor and the department, as the amount is minor.","hi":"राशि कम होने के कारण अपने मार्गदर्शक और विभाग की रक्षा के लिए निष्कर्षों को अनदेखा कर दें।"},"2":{"en":"Submit an anonymous report to the internal compliance team to remove your personal involvement while ensuring the issue is resolved.","hi":"स्वयं को व्यक्तिगत रूप से दूर रखते हुए मामला सुलझाने के लिए आंतरिक अनुपालन टीम को गुप्त रिपोर्ट भेजें।"},"3":{"en":"Arrange a private meeting to present audit evidence objectively, allowing the manager to explain before finalising the documentation.","hi":"निजी बैठक करके अंकेक्षण के प्रमाण वस्तुनिष्ठ रूप से प्रस्तुत करें और दस्तावेज़ अंतिम रूप देने से पहले प्रबंधक को स्पष्टीकरण का अवसर दें।"},"4":{"en":"Confront the manager in a team meeting to show everyone that no one is above the rules.","hi":"टीम बैठक में प्रबंधक से आमना-सामना करें ताकि सब देखें कि कोई नियमों से ऊपर नहीं है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Ignoring the finding breaks the auditor's duty, and an anonymous report neither allows an explanation nor keeps the trust of a mentor<br>Presenting the evidence privately and objectively is honest, gives the manager a fair chance to respond and protects the process<br>Public confrontation humiliates a senior colleague and damages the department<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Arrange a private meeting to present audit evidence objectively, allowing the manager to explain before finalising the documentation.</b>","hi":"निष्कर्षों को अनदेखा करना अंकेक्षक के कर्तव्य का उल्लंघन है और गुप्त रिपोर्ट से न तो स्पष्टीकरण मिलता है और न ही मार्गदर्शक का विश्वास बना रहता है<br>प्रमाण निजी और वस्तुनिष्ठ रूप से प्रस्तुत करना ईमानदार है, प्रबंधक को उचित अवसर देता है और प्रक्रिया की रक्षा करता है<br>सार्वजनिक टकराव वरिष्ठ सहकर्मी का अपमान करता है और विभाग को हानि पहुँचाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): निजी बैठक करके अंकेक्षण के प्रमाण वस्तुनिष्ठ रूप से प्रस्तुत करें और दस्तावेज़ अंतिम रूप देने से पहले प्रबंधक को स्पष्टीकरण का अवसर दें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000073901","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Read the given conditions carefully and determine the appropriate outcome for the case provided.<br><b>Criteria for Admission to Executive MBA:</b><br>1. The candidate must have a bachelor's degree with at least fifty percent marks.<br>2. The candidate must have at least five years of managerial experience.<br>3. The candidate must provide two letters of recommendation from current employers.<br><b>Exception:</b> If the candidate has ten years of experience, only one recommendation letter is required.<br><b>Case:</b> Sunita has a bachelor's degree with 55% marks and 12 years of managerial experience. She has submitted one recommendation letter. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई शर्तों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और दिए गए मामले के लिए उपयुक्त परिणाम निर्धारित कीजिए।<br><b>कार्यकारी एमबीए में प्रवेश के मानदंड:</b><br>1. अभ्यर्थी के पास कम से कम पचास प्रतिशत अंकों के साथ स्नातक डिग्री होनी चाहिए।<br>2. अभ्यर्थी के पास कम से कम पाँच वर्ष का प्रबंधकीय अनुभव होना चाहिए।<br>3. अभ्यर्थी को वर्तमान नियोक्ताओं से दो अनुशंसा पत्र प्रदान करने होंगे।<br><b>अपवाद:</b> यदि अभ्यर्थी के पास दस वर्ष का अनुभव है, तो केवल एक अनुशंसा पत्र आवश्यक है।<br><b>मामला:</b> सुनीता के पास 55% अंकों के साथ स्नातक डिग्री और 12 वर्ष का प्रबंधकीय अनुभव है। उसने एक अनुशंसा पत्र जमा किया है। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Admitted","hi":"प्रवेश दिया जाए"},"2":{"en":"Not Admitted","hi":"प्रवेश नहीं दिया जाए"},"3":{"en":"Data Inadequate","hi":"आँकड़े अपर्याप्त"},"4":{"en":"Application Pending Review","hi":"आवेदन समीक्षा हेतु लंबित"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The degree has 55% marks, which is above fifty percent ✔, and the experience of 12 years is more than five years ✔<br>Her experience is also above ten years, so under the exception only one recommendation letter is needed ✔<br>All conditions are satisfied, so she should be admitted<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Admitted.</b>","hi":"डिग्री में 55% अंक हैं, जो पचास प्रतिशत से अधिक हैं ✔, तथा 12 वर्ष का अनुभव पाँच वर्ष से अधिक है ✔<br>उसका अनुभव दस वर्ष से भी अधिक है, अतः अपवाद के अनुसार केवल एक अनुशंसा पत्र पर्याप्त है ✔<br>सभी शर्तें पूरी हैं, अतः उसे प्रवेश दिया जाए<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): प्रवेश दिया जाए है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000073902","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word.<br>Melt : Liquid :: Freeze : ? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प का चयन कीजिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है।<br>Melt : Liquid :: Freeze : ? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ice","hi":"बर्फ़"},"2":{"en":"Solid","hi":"ठोस"},"3":{"en":"Vapor","hi":"वाष्प"},"4":{"en":"Condense","hi":"संघनित होना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Melting changes a substance into the liquid state<br>Freezing changes a substance into the solid state<br>So the answer is solid<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Solid.</b>","hi":"पिघलने से पदार्थ द्रव अवस्था में बदल जाता है<br>जमने से पदार्थ ठोस अवस्था में बदल जाता है<br>अतः उत्तर ठोस है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ठोस है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000073903","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A national environmental authority has restricted industrial discharge into river systems following reports of deteriorating aquatic biodiversity.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Industrial discharge contributes to water pollution.<br>II. Aquatic ecosystems are under environmental stress. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों को देखिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा निष्कर्ष तार्किक रूप से कथन से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>जलीय जैव विविधता में गिरावट की रिपोर्टों के बाद एक राष्ट्रीय पर्यावरण प्राधिकरण ने नदी प्रणालियों में औद्योगिक निर्वहन प्रतिबंधित किया है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. औद्योगिक निर्वहन जल प्रदूषण में योगदान देता है।<br>II. जलीय पारिस्थितिक तंत्र पर्यावरणीय दबाव में है। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A restriction on industrial discharge was imposed because such discharge harms the rivers, so I follows<br>The report of deteriorating aquatic biodiversity itself shows environmental stress on aquatic ecosystems, so II follows<br>Hence both conclusions follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Both conclusions I and II follow.</b>","hi":"औद्योगिक निर्वहन पर प्रतिबंध इसलिए लगाया गया क्योंकि ऐसा निर्वहन नदियों को हानि पहुँचाता है, अतः I निकलता है<br>जलीय जैव विविधता में गिरावट की रिपोर्ट ही जलीय पारिस्थितिक तंत्र पर पर्यावरणीय दबाव दर्शाती है, अतः II निकलता है<br>इसलिए दोनों निष्कर्ष निकलते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000073904","section":"REASONING","topic":"Direction & Distance","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word.<br>North-East : South :: South-East : ? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प का चयन कीजिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है।<br>North-East : South :: South-East : ? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"West","hi":"पश्चिम"},"2":{"en":"North-West","hi":"उत्तर-पश्चिम"},"3":{"en":"North-East","hi":"उत्तर-पूर्व"},"4":{"en":"East","hi":"पूर्व"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"North-East becomes South when the direction is turned 135° clockwise<br>Applying the same 135° clockwise turn to South-East gives West<br>So the answer is West<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): West.</b>","hi":"उत्तर-पूर्व दिशा को 135° दक्षिणावर्त घुमाने पर दक्षिण मिलता है<br>वही 135° दक्षिणावर्त घुमाव दक्षिण-पूर्व पर लगाने से पश्चिम मिलता है<br>अतः उत्तर पश्चिम है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): पश्चिम है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000073905","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Unless the government provides direct financial assistance to small-scale farmers for crop insurance, the migration of rural labor to urban centers will continue unabated.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Financial instability due to crop failure is a primary driver of rural-to-urban migration.<br>II. Crop insurance is the only mechanism that can prevent labor migration. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिया गया कथन ध्यान से पढ़िए और उस पर आधारित अनुमानों को देखिए। निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-से अनुमान कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>जब तक सरकार फ़सल बीमा के लिए छोटे किसानों को सीधी वित्तीय सहायता नहीं देती, ग्रामीण श्रमिकों का शहरी केंद्रों की ओर पलायन बिना रुके जारी रहेगा।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. फ़सल खराब होने से उत्पन्न वित्तीय अस्थिरता ग्रामीण-से-शहरी पलायन का प्रमुख कारण है।<br>II. फ़सल बीमा ही एकमात्र तंत्र है जो श्रम पलायन रोक सकता है। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निहित है"},"3":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अनुमान I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अनुमान I और न ही II निहित है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The statement links financial help for crop insurance with stopping migration, which is meaningful only if money problems caused by crop failure drive the migration, so I is implicit<br>It says 'unless', not that insurance is the only way, so II is too strong and is not implicit<br>Hence only assumption I is implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Assumption I is implicit.</b>","hi":"कथन फ़सल बीमा के लिए वित्तीय सहायता को पलायन रोकने से जोड़ता है, जो तभी अर्थपूर्ण है जब फ़सल खराबी से उत्पन्न धन की समस्या पलायन का कारण हो, अतः I निहित है<br>कथन 'जब तक' कहता है, यह नहीं कि बीमा ही एकमात्र उपाय है, अतः II अति है और निहित नहीं<br>इसलिए केवल अनुमान I निहित है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल अनुमान I निहित है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000073906","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"The Human Development Index (HDI) uses logarithmic transformation for Gross National Income (GNI) per capita, and aims to: [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मानव विकास सूचकांक (HDI) प्रति व्यक्ति सकल राष्ट्रीय आय (GNI) हेतु लघुगणकीय रूपांतरण का प्रयोग करता है, जिसका उद्देश्य है: [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Reduce the impact of extremely high incomes.","hi":"अत्यधिक उच्च आय के प्रभाव को घटाना।"},"2":{"en":"Give more weight to higher incomes.","hi":"उच्च आय को अधिक भार देना।"},"3":{"en":"Exclude income from natural resource extraction.","hi":"प्राकृतिक संसाधन निष्कर्षण से प्राप्त आय को बाहर रखना।"},"4":{"en":"Adjust for inflation.","hi":"मुद्रास्फीति हेतु समायोजन करना।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Reduce the impact of extremely high incomes</b><br>The HDI applies a <b>logarithmic transformation</b> to GNI per capita so that the <b>influence of extremely high incomes is reduced</b> and each extra unit of income adds less and less to the index. This reflects the diminishing returns of income to human development.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The HDI has three dimensions - <b>health</b> (life expectancy at birth), <b>education</b> (mean and expected years of schooling) and <b>standard of living</b> (GNI per capita PPP).<br>• The index is the <b>geometric mean</b> of the three dimension indices, each scaled between 0 and 1, and is published by <b>UNDP</b>.<br>• Without the logarithmic transformation a very rich country would dominate the index, so logs give a <b>diminishing weight</b> to higher income.<br>• <b>Inflation</b> is handled by using constant prices and <b>natural resource income</b> is not excluded, which is why the other options are wrong.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अत्यधिक उच्च आय के प्रभाव को घटाना।</b><br>HDI प्रति व्यक्ति GNI पर <b>लघुगणकीय रूपांतरण</b> इसलिए लागू करता है कि <b>अत्यधिक उच्च आय का प्रभाव घट जाए</b> और आय की प्रत्येक अतिरिक्त इकाई सूचकांक में क्रमशः कम जोड़े। यह मानव विकास हेतु आय के घटते प्रतिफल को दर्शाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• HDI के तीन आयाम हैं - <b>स्वास्थ्य</b> (जन्म पर जीवन प्रत्याशा), <b>शिक्षा</b> (औसत व अपेक्षित स्कूली वर्ष) तथा <b>जीवन-स्तर</b> (प्रति व्यक्ति GNI PPP)।<br>• सूचकांक तीन आयाम सूचकांकों का <b>ज्यामितीय माध्य</b> है, जिनमें प्रत्येक 0 से 1 के बीच मापा जाता है, और इसे <b>UNDP</b> प्रकाशित करता है।<br>• लघुगणकीय रूपांतरण के बिना कोई अत्यधिक धनी देश सूचकांक पर हावी हो जाता, इसलिए लॉग उच्च आय को <b>घटता भार</b> देते हैं।<br>• <b>मुद्रास्फीति</b> का समायोजन स्थिर कीमतों से होता है तथा <b>प्राकृतिक संसाधन आय</b> को बाहर नहीं रखा जाता, इसीलिए शेष विकल्प गलत हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000073907","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"The concept of \"secondary pollutants\" in the Air Quality Index (AQI) is best illustrated by: [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वायु गुणवत्ता सूचकांक (AQI) में \"द्वितीयक प्रदूषक\" की अवधारणा का सर्वोत्तम उदाहरण है: [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Direct emissions of particulate matter from industrial sources.","hi":"औद्योगिक स्रोतों से कण पदार्थों का प्रत्यक्ष उत्सर्जन।"},"2":{"en":"Sulfur dioxide emitted from power plants.","hi":"विद्युत संयंत्रों से उत्सर्जित सल्फर डाइऑक्साइड।"},"3":{"en":"Ozone formed from the interaction of NOx and VOCs.","hi":"NOx व VOC की अंतःक्रिया से बनने वाला ओज़ोन।"},"4":{"en":"Carbon monoxide from vehicle exhaust.","hi":"वाहन निकास से कार्बन मोनोऑक्साइड।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Ozone formed from the interaction of NOx and VOCs</b><br>A <b>secondary pollutant</b> is not emitted directly but is formed in the atmosphere by chemical reactions between primary pollutants. <b>Ground-level ozone</b> is the classic example, produced when <b>nitrogen oxides (NOx)</b> and <b>volatile organic compounds (VOCs)</b> react in sunlight.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Primary pollutants</b> such as sulphur dioxide, carbon monoxide and particulate matter are released directly from sources like vehicles, power plants and industry.<br>• Other secondary pollutants are <b>peroxyacetyl nitrate (PAN)</b>, nitric acid, sulphuric acid and secondary organic aerosols, which form photochemical smog.<br>• The <b>AQI</b> in India is computed for eight pollutants - <b>PM10, PM2.5, NO2, SO2, CO, O3, NH3 and Pb</b> - and has six categories from Good to Severe.<br>• <b>Photochemical smog</b> over cities such as Delhi is largely a secondary pollution problem formed in sunlight.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – NOx व VOC की अंतःक्रिया से बनने वाला ओज़ोन।</b><br><b>द्वितीयक प्रदूषक</b> सीधे उत्सर्जित नहीं होता, बल्कि वायुमंडल में प्राथमिक प्रदूषकों के बीच रासायनिक अभिक्रिया से बनता है। <b>भू-स्तरीय ओज़ोन</b> इसका प्रमुख उदाहरण है, जो सूर्य के प्रकाश में <b>नाइट्रोजन ऑक्साइड (NOx)</b> तथा <b>वाष्पशील कार्बनिक यौगिकों (VOC)</b> की अभिक्रिया से बनता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सल्फर डाइऑक्साइड, कार्बन मोनोऑक्साइड तथा कण पदार्थ जैसे <b>प्राथमिक प्रदूषक</b> वाहनों, विद्युत संयंत्रों व उद्योगों से सीधे निकलते हैं।<br>• अन्य द्वितीयक प्रदूषक <b>पेरॉक्सीएसिटिल नाइट्रेट (PAN)</b>, नाइट्रिक अम्ल, सल्फ्यूरिक अम्ल तथा द्वितीयक कार्बनिक एरोसोल हैं, जो प्रकाश-रासायनिक स्मॉग बनाते हैं।<br>• भारत में <b>AQI</b> आठ प्रदूषकों - <b>PM10, PM2.5, NO2, SO2, CO, O3, NH3 तथा Pb</b> - हेतु निकाला जाता है और इसकी छह श्रेणियाँ अच्छी से गंभीर तक हैं।<br>• दिल्ली जैसे शहरों में <b>प्रकाश-रासायनिक स्मॉग</b> मुख्यतः द्वितीयक प्रदूषण की समस्या है, जो सूर्य के प्रकाश में बनती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000073908","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"The name of the lander used in Chandrayaan-3 mission is: [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"चंद्रयान-3 मिशन में प्रयुक्त लैंडर का नाम है: [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Aryabhata","hi":"आर्यभट"},"2":{"en":"Mangal","hi":"मंगल"},"3":{"en":"Pragyan","hi":"प्रज्ञान"},"4":{"en":"Vikram","hi":"विक्रम"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Vikram</b><br>The <b>Chandrayaan-3</b> lander was named <b>Vikram</b>, after Dr Vikram Sarabhai, the father of the Indian space programme. It carried the <b>Pragyan</b> rover.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Chandrayaan-3 was launched on <b>14 July 2023</b> by the <b>LVM3-M4</b> rocket and landed near the lunar south pole on <b>23 August 2023</b>.<br>• India became the <b>first country to land near the lunar south pole</b> and the <b>fourth to soft-land on the Moon</b> after the USA, USSR and China.<br>• The lander carried the instruments <b>ChaSTE, ILSA, RAMBHA-LP and LRA</b>, and the mission detected sulphur and other elements in the soil.<br>• <b>23 August</b> is now observed as <b>National Space Day</b>, and <b>Pragyan</b> means wisdom in Sanskrit.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – विक्रम</b><br><b>चंद्रयान-3</b> के लैंडर का नाम भारतीय अंतरिक्ष कार्यक्रम के जनक डॉ. विक्रम साराभाई के नाम पर <b>विक्रम</b> रखा गया। इसके साथ <b>प्रज्ञान</b> रोवर भेजा गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• चंद्रयान-3 का प्रक्षेपण <b>14 जुलाई 2023</b> को <b>LVM3-M4</b> रॉकेट से हुआ और यह <b>23 अगस्त 2023</b> को चंद्र दक्षिणी ध्रुव के निकट उतरा।<br>• भारत <b>चंद्र दक्षिणी ध्रुव के निकट उतरने वाला पहला देश</b> तथा अमेरिका, सोवियत संघ व चीन के बाद <b>चंद्रमा पर सॉफ्ट लैंडिंग करने वाला चौथा देश</b> बना।<br>• लैंडर में <b>ChaSTE, ILSA, RAMBHA-LP तथा LRA</b> उपकरण थे और मिशन ने मिट्टी में गंधक व अन्य तत्वों की पहचान की।<br>• अब <b>23 अगस्त</b> को <b>राष्ट्रीय अंतरिक्ष दिवस</b> मनाया जाता है; संस्कृत में <b>प्रज्ञान</b> का अर्थ बुद्धि है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000073909","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"Which ISRO mission is focused on Earth observation to monitor climate and environmental changes? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा इसरो मिशन जलवायु व पर्यावरणीय परिवर्तनों की निगरानी हेतु भू-प्रेक्षण पर केंद्रित है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RISAT series","hi":"रिसैट श्रृंखला"},"2":{"en":"Mangalyaan","hi":"मंगलयान"},"3":{"en":"Gaganyaan","hi":"गगनयान"},"4":{"en":"Chandrayaan-1","hi":"चंद्रयान-1"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – RISAT series</b><br>The <b>RISAT (Radar Imaging Satellite)</b> series is an ISRO <b>Earth observation</b> programme that uses synthetic aperture radar for <b>remote sensing, disaster management and monitoring of climate and environmental change</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>RISAT-1</b>, launched in 2012, was India's first indigenous radar imaging satellite with a C-band SAR payload, and it works <b>day and night through clouds</b>.<br>• Other ISRO Earth observation series are <b>IRS, Cartosat, Resourcesat, Oceansat and INSAT-3DR</b> for weather and climate studies.<br>• <b>Mangalyaan</b> was the Mars Orbiter Mission of 2013 and <b>Chandrayaan-1</b> the 2008 lunar mission, while <b>Gaganyaan</b> is the human spaceflight programme.<br>• Radar imaging is valuable for flood mapping, crop monitoring, soil moisture and cyclone damage assessment, as it is not blocked by cloud cover.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – रिसैट श्रृंखला</b><br><b>रिसैट (रडार इमेजिंग सैटेलाइट)</b> श्रृंखला इसरो का <b>भू-प्रेक्षण</b> कार्यक्रम है, जिसमें सिंथेटिक एपर्चर रडार के माध्यम से <b>दूरसंवेदन, आपदा प्रबंधन तथा जलवायु व पर्यावरणीय परिवर्तन की निगरानी</b> होती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 2012 में प्रक्षेपित <b>RISAT-1</b> C-बैंड SAR पेलोड वाला भारत का पहला स्वदेशी रडार इमेजिंग उपग्रह था, जो <b>दिन-रात तथा बादलों के बीच भी</b> कार्य करता है।<br>• इसरो की अन्य भू-प्रेक्षण श्रृंखलाएँ <b>IRS, कार्टोसैट, रिसोर्ससैट, ओशनसैट तथा मौसम हेतु INSAT-3DR</b> हैं।<br>• <b>मंगलयान</b> 2013 का मंगल ऑर्बिटर मिशन तथा <b>चंद्रयान-1</b> 2008 का चंद्र मिशन था, जबकि <b>गगनयान</b> मानव अंतरिक्ष उड़ान कार्यक्रम है।<br>• रडार इमेजिंग बाढ़ मानचित्रण, फसल निगरानी, मृदा नमी तथा चक्रवाती क्षति आकलन हेतु उपयोगी है, क्योंकि बादल इसे रोक नहीं सकते।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000073910","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Delhi Sultanate","question":{"en":"In which year did Timur invade India, plundering Delhi? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"तैमूर ने किस वर्ष भारत पर आक्रमण कर दिल्ली को लूटा? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1398 CE","hi":"1398 ईस्वी"},"2":{"en":"1401 CE","hi":"1401 ईस्वी"},"3":{"en":"1389 CE","hi":"1389 ईस्वी"},"4":{"en":"1405 CE","hi":"1405 ईस्वी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 1398 CE</b><br><b>Timur (Tamerlane)</b> invaded India in <b>1398 CE</b> during the reign of Sultan <b>Nasir-ud-din Mahmud Shah Tughlaq</b>, defeated his army near Delhi, and plundered and massacred the city for several days.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Timur was the ruler of <b>Samarkand</b> and founder of the Timurid empire; he claimed to invade India to punish the Tughlaq rulers for their leniency towards Hindus.<br>• He took away enormous wealth, including the famous <b>Koh-i-Noor</b> diamond, and appointed <b>Khizr Khan</b> as governor of the region.<br>• The invasion exposed the weakness of the <b>Tughlaq dynasty</b> and hastened the end of the Sultanate, leading to the rise of the <b>Sayyid dynasty</b> in 1414.<br>• Timur died in <b>1405 CE</b> while on his way to invade China, and his descendant Babur later founded the <b>Mughal empire</b> in India.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – 1398 ईस्वी</b><br><b>तैमूर (तैमूरलंग)</b> ने सुल्तान <b>नासिरुद्दीन महमूद शाह तुगलक</b> के शासनकाल में <b>1398 ईस्वी</b> में भारत पर आक्रमण किया, दिल्ली के निकट उसकी सेना को पराजित किया तथा कई दिनों तक नगर को लूटा और नरसंहार किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• तैमूर <b>समरकंद</b> का शासक तथा तैमूरी साम्राज्य का संस्थापक था; उसने तुगलक शासकों की उदारता को दंडित करने का बहाना बनाकर आक्रमण किया।<br>• वह अपार धन, जिसमें प्रसिद्ध <b>कोहिनूर</b> हीरा सम्मिलित था, ले गया और <b>खिज्र खान</b> को शासक नियुक्त किया।<br>• इस आक्रमण ने <b>तुगलक वंश</b> की कमजोरी उजागर की और सल्तनत का अंत तेज किया; 1414 में <b>सैयद वंश</b> सत्ता में आया।<br>• तैमूर की मृत्यु <b>1405 ईस्वी</b> में चीन पर आक्रमण के मार्ग में हुई, और उसी के वंशज बाबर ने भारत में बाद में <b>मुगल साम्राज्य</b> स्थापित किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000073911","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"Which of the following constituted the core thrust areas of the Rolling Plan (1978-1980), which superseded the Fifth Five-Year Plan in its policy orientation? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से क्या रोलिंग योजना (1978-1980) के मुख्य केंद्रित क्षेत्र थे, जिसने अपनी नीतिगत दिशा में पाँचवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना का स्थान लिया? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rural development and social welfare programme","hi":"ग्रामीण विकास तथा समाज कल्याण कार्यक्रम"},"2":{"en":"Space technology development","hi":"अंतरिक्ष प्रौद्योगिकी विकास"},"3":{"en":"Strategic disinvestment and privatization of state-owned enterprises","hi":"सार्वजनिक उपक्रमों का रणनीतिक विनिवेश एवं निजीकरण"},"4":{"en":"Promotion of outward-looking, export-driven economic strategies","hi":"बहिर्मुखी, निर्यात-प्रेरित आर्थिक रणनीतियों को बढ़ावा"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Rural development and social welfare programme</b><br>The <b>Rolling Plan (1978-1980)</b> of the Janata government replaced the Fifth Five-Year Plan in its policy orientation, and its core thrust was on <b>rural development, employment generation and social welfare</b> programmes.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Rolling Plan concept was proposed by <b>Gunnar Myrdal</b>; the plan was revised every year with a fresh annual plan, a three-year perspective and a long-term perspective.<br>• It emphasised <b>agriculture, rural industries, khadi and village industries</b> and programmes such as food-for-work and the <b>Antyodaya</b> scheme.<br>• The <b>Fifth Five-Year Plan (1974-79)</b> had targeted <b>removal of poverty (Garibi Hatao)</b> and self-reliance, and it was terminated one year early in 1978.<br>• The Sixth Plan (1980-85) later returned to the regular five-year framework and laid emphasis on poverty alleviation and employment.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – ग्रामीण विकास तथा समाज कल्याण कार्यक्रम</b><br>जनता सरकार की <b>रोलिंग योजना (1978-1980)</b> ने नीतिगत दिशा में पाँचवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना का स्थान लिया, और इसका मुख्य बल <b>ग्रामीण विकास, रोजगार सृजन तथा समाज कल्याण</b> कार्यक्रमों पर था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• रोलिंग योजना की संकल्पना <b>गुन्नार मिर्डाल</b> ने प्रस्तुत की; इसमें प्रत्येक वर्ष नई वार्षिक योजना, त्रिवर्षीय परिप्रेक्ष्य तथा दीर्घकालिक परिप्रेक्ष्य के साथ योजना संशोधित होती थी।<br>• इसमें <b>कृषि, ग्रामीण उद्योग, खादी व ग्रामोद्योग</b> तथा कार्य-के-बदले-अनाज और <b>अंत्योदय</b> जैसे कार्यक्रमों पर बल दिया गया।<br>• <b>पाँचवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना (1974-79)</b> का लक्ष्य <b>गरीबी उन्मूलन (गरीबी हटाओ)</b> तथा आत्मनिर्भरता था और इसे 1978 में एक वर्ष पूर्व समाप्त कर दिया गया।<br>• छठी योजना (1980-85) ने बाद में सामान्य पंचवर्षीय ढाँचे की ओर लौटते हुए गरीबी उपशमन व रोजगार पर बल दिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000073912","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Awards and Honours","question":{"en":"Which Tanzanian-born British author won the Nobel Prize in Literature in <b>2021</b>? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>2021</b> में साहित्य का नोबेल पुरस्कार किस तंजानिया में जन्मे ब्रिटिश लेखक ने जीता? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Abdulrazak Gurnah","hi":"अब्दुलरज्ज़ाक गुरनाह"},"2":{"en":"Chinua Achebe","hi":"चिनुआ अचेबे"},"3":{"en":"Ngugi wa Thiong'o","hi":"न्गुगी वा थियोंगो"},"4":{"en":"Ben Okri","hi":"बेन ओकरी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Abdulrazak Gurnah</b><br><b>Abdulrazak Gurnah</b>, born in Zanzibar and based in Britain, won the <b>Nobel Prize in Literature 2021</b> for his uncompromising and compassionate portrayal of the effects of <b>colonialism and migration</b> on the lives of refugees.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• His best-known novels are <b>Paradise</b>, <b>By the Sea</b>, <b>Desertion</b> and <b>Afterlives</b>; <b>Paradise</b> was shortlisted for the Booker Prize in 1994.<br>• <b>Chinua Achebe</b> of Nigeria wrote <b>Things Fall Apart</b>, and <b>Ben Okri</b> won the Booker Prize in 1991 for <b>The Famished Road</b>.<br>• <b>Ngugi wa Thiong'o</b> is a Kenyan writer known for <b>Weep Not, Child</b> and <b>Petals of Blood</b>.<br>• The Nobel Prize in Literature is awarded by the <b>Swedish Academy</b>, and the 2021 award was announced in October 2021.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अब्दुलरज्ज़ाक गुरनाह</b><br>ज़ांज़ीबार में जन्मे तथा ब्रिटेन में रहने वाले <b>अब्दुलरज्ज़ाक गुरनाह</b> को <b>2021 का साहित्य नोबेल पुरस्कार</b> मिला, जिसका कारण <b>उपनिवेशवाद व प्रवासन</b> के शरणार्थियों के जीवन पर पड़ने वाले प्रभाव का उनका निर्मम व करुण चित्रण था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उनके प्रसिद्ध उपन्यास <b>पैराडाइज़</b>, <b>बाय द सी</b>, <b>डेज़र्शन</b> तथा <b>आफ्टरलाइव्स</b> हैं; <b>पैराडाइज़</b> 1994 में बुकर पुरस्कार हेतु चयनित हुआ था।<br>• नाइजीरिया के <b>चिनुआ अचेबे</b> ने <b>थिंग्स फॉल अप्रार्ट</b> लिखी, तथा <b>बेन ओकरी</b> ने 1991 में <b>द फैमिश्ड रोड</b> हेतु बुकर पुरस्कार जीता।<br>• <b>न्गुगी वा थियोंगो</b> केन्या के लेखक हैं, जो <b>वीप नॉट, चाइल्ड</b> तथा <b>पेटल्स ऑफ ब्लड</b> के लिए जाने जाते हैं।<br>• साहित्य का नोबेल पुरस्कार <b>स्वीडिश अकादमी</b> देती है और 2021 का पुरस्कार अक्टूबर 2021 में घोषित हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000073913","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Who won the first medal for India at the <b>2020</b> Tokyo Olympics? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>2020</b> टोक्यो ओलंपिक में भारत हेतु पहला पदक किसने जीता? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ravi Kumar Dahiya","hi":"रवि कुमार दहिया"},"2":{"en":"Mirabai Chanu","hi":"मीराबाई चानू"},"3":{"en":"PV Sindhu","hi":"पी.वी. सिंधु"},"4":{"en":"Bajrang Punia","hi":"बजरंग पूनिया"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Mirabai Chanu</b><br><b>Mirabai Chanu</b> won India's <b>first medal</b> at the <b>Tokyo 2020 Olympics</b>, a <b>silver in weightlifting</b> in the <b>49 kg category</b>, which opened India's account at the Games.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India won <b>seven medals</b> at Tokyo 2020 - one gold, two silver and four bronze - its best tally till then.<br>• <b>Neeraj Chopra</b> won the <b>gold in javelin throw</b>, the first Olympic gold for India in athletics, and <b>PV Sindhu</b> won a bronze in badminton.<br>• <b>Ravi Kumar Dahiya</b> won silver in wrestling, and <b>Bajrang Punia</b> won bronze in wrestling; the men's hockey team also won bronze after 41 years.<br>• <b>Mirabai Chanu</b> is from Manipur and was awarded the <b>Padma Shri</b> and the Rajiv Gandhi Khel Ratna.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मीराबाई चानू</b><br><b>मीराबाई चानू</b> ने <b>टोक्यो 2020 ओलंपिक</b> में भारत का <b>पहला पदक</b> जीता - <b>49 किग्रा वर्ग</b> में भारोत्तोलन का <b>रजत</b>, जिससे भारत का खाता खुला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• टोक्यो 2020 में भारत ने <b>सात पदक</b> - एक स्वर्ण, दो रजत तथा चार कांस्य - जीते, जो तब तक का सर्वश्रेष्ठ प्रदर्शन था।<br>• <b>नीरज चोपड़ा</b> ने <b>भाला फेंक में स्वर्ण</b> जीता, जो एथलेटिक्स में भारत का पहला ओलंपिक स्वर्ण था, तथा <b>पी.वी. सिंधु</b> ने बैडमिंटन में कांस्य जीता।<br>• <b>रवि कुमार दहिया</b> ने कुश्ती में रजत तथा <b>बजरंग पूनिया</b> ने कांस्य जीता; पुरुष हॉकी टीम ने भी 41 वर्ष बाद कांस्य जीता।<br>• <b>मीराबाई चानू</b> मणिपुर की हैं और उन्हें <b>पद्म श्री</b> तथा राजीव गांधी खेल रत्न से सम्मानित किया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000073914","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"Which tribe celebrates the Nagoba Jatara festival in Telangana? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"तेलंगाना में नागोबा जातरा उत्सव कौन-सी जनजाति मनाती है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gond","hi":"गोंड"},"2":{"en":"Lambadi","hi":"लंबाडी"},"3":{"en":"Banjara","hi":"बंजारा"},"4":{"en":"Koya","hi":"कोया"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Gond</b><br><b>Nagoba Jatara</b> is a major tribal festival of the <b>Gond</b> tribe, held at <b>Keslapur in Adilabad district of Telangana</b> in the month of <b>Magh</b>, and it is one of the largest tribal fairs of the state.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The festival is dedicated to the serpent deity <b>Nagoba</b> and is celebrated by the Gond, Pardhan and Kolam communities, who take out a large procession and perform the <b>Gussadi dance</b>.<br>• The <b>Gond</b> are one of the largest tribal groups in India and are spread across Telangana, Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Maharashtra and Odisha.<br>• <b>Lambadi</b> (Banjara) and <b>Koya</b> are other important tribes of Telangana; the Koya live mainly in the Godavari basin and speak Koya, a Dravidian language.<br>• Telangana's other well-known festivals are <b>Bathukamma</b> and <b>Bonalu</b>, and the Sammakka-Saralakka Jatara is held at Medaram.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – गोंड</b><br><b>नागोबा जातरा</b> <b>गोंड</b> जनजाति का प्रमुख उत्सव है, जो <b>तेलंगाना के आदिलाबाद जिले के केसलापुर</b> में <b>माघ</b> मास में आयोजित होता है और राज्य के सबसे बड़े जनजातीय मेलों में से एक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह उत्सव नाग देवता <b>नागोबा</b> को समर्पित है और इसे गोंड, पर्धान तथा कोलम समुदाय मनाते हैं, जिसमें बड़ी शोभायात्रा निकलती है एवं <b>गुसाड़ी नृत्य</b> किया जाता है।<br>• <b>गोंड</b> भारत की सबसे बड़ी जनजातियों में है और तेलंगाना, मध्य प्रदेश, छत्तीसगढ़, महाराष्ट्र व ओडिशा में फैली है।<br>• <b>लंबाडी</b> (बंजारा) तथा <b>कोया</b> तेलंगाना की अन्य प्रमुख जनजातियाँ हैं; कोया मुख्यतः गोदावरी बेसिन में रहते हैं और कोया भाषा (द्रविड़) बोलते हैं।<br>• तेलंगाना के अन्य प्रसिद्ध उत्सव <b>बथुकम्मा</b> व <b>बोनालु</b> हैं, तथा सम्मक्का-सारलम्मा जातरा मेडारम में होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000073915","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The primary aim of the \"Arms Act\" passed by the British government in <b>1878</b> was to: [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>1878</b> में ब्रिटिश सरकार द्वारा पारित \"शस्त्र अधिनियम\" का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य था: [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Encourage Indians to join the British Indian Army.","hi":"भारतीयों को ब्रिटिश भारतीय सेना में भर्ती होने हेतु प्रोत्साहित करना।"},"2":{"en":"Regulate the manufacturing and sale of firearms by Europeans in India.","hi":"भारत में यूरोपीय लोगों द्वारा हथियार निर्माण एवं बिक्री का नियमन करना।"},"3":{"en":"Prevent Indians from possessing firearms without a license.","hi":"भारतीयों को बिना लाइसेंस हथियार रखने से रोकना।"},"4":{"en":"Promote the development of indigenous arms manufacturing in India.","hi":"भारत में स्वदेशी शस्त्र निर्माण के विकास को बढ़ावा देना।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Prevent Indians from possessing firearms without a license.</b><br>The <b>Indian Arms Act of 1878</b> was passed to <b>disarm the Indian population</b> by making a licence compulsory for possessing, manufacturing or selling firearms, while Europeans were largely exempt from it.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Act followed the <b>Revolt of 1857</b> and was part of the policy of keeping Indians disarmed.<br>• It restricted the possession of <b>arms of every description</b> and empowered the government to refuse or cancel licences.<br>• <b>Lord Lytton</b> was the Viceroy when the Act was passed, and it came in the same year as the <b>Vernacular Press Act, 1878</b>.<br>• The Act remained in force in independent India and was replaced by the <b>Arms Act, 1959</b>, which continues to regulate gun licences.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – भारतीयों को बिना लाइसेंस हथियार रखने से रोकना।</b><br><b>1878 का भारतीय शस्त्र अधिनियम</b> भारतीय जनता को <b>निःशस्त्र</b> करने हेतु पारित हुआ; इसके अनुसार हथियार रखने, बनाने या बेचने हेतु लाइसेंस अनिवार्य हो गया, जबकि यूरोपीय लोगों को इसमें मोटे तौर पर छूट थी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह अधिनियम <b>1857 के विद्रोह</b> के बाद आया और भारतीयों को निःशस्त्र रखने की नीति का भाग था।<br>• इसने <b>सभी प्रकार के शस्त्रों</b> को रखने पर प्रतिबंध लगाया और सरकार को लाइसेंस अस्वीकार करने या रद्द करने की शक्ति दी।<br>• अधिनियम पारित होने के समय <b>लॉर्ड लिटन</b> वायसराय थे, और उसी वर्ष <b>वर्नाक्युलर प्रेस अधिनियम, 1878</b> भी पारित हुआ।<br>• यह अधिनियम स्वतंत्र भारत में भी लागू रहा और इसका स्थान <b>शस्त्र अधिनियम, 1959</b> ने लिया, जो आज भी बंदूक लाइसेंस का नियमन करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000073916","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"In September <b>2022</b>, who was named to serve as the Director General of the Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR)? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>सितंबर 2022</b> में भारतीय आयुर्विज्ञान अनुसंधान परिषद (ICMR) के महानिदेशक के रूप में किसे नियुक्त किया गया? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Dr. Soumya Swaminathan","hi":"डॉ. सौम्या स्वामीनाथन"},"2":{"en":"Dr. Priya Abraham","hi":"डॉ. प्रिया अब्राहम"},"3":{"en":"Dr. Rajiv Bahl","hi":"डॉ. राजीव बहल"},"4":{"en":"Dr. Nivedita Gupta","hi":"डॉ. निवेदिता गुप्ता"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Dr. Rajiv Bahl</b><br><b>Dr Rajiv Bahl</b> was appointed <b>Director General of the ICMR</b> and Secretary, Department of Health Research, in <b>September 2022</b>. He earlier worked with the <b>World Health Organization</b> on immunisation and child health.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>ICMR</b> was founded in <b>1911</b> as the Indian Research Fund Association and was renamed the Indian Council of Medical Research in <b>1949</b>; its headquarters is in <b>New Delhi</b>.<br>• It is the apex body for the formulation, coordination and promotion of <b>biomedical research</b> in India and functions under the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare.<br>• <b>Dr Soumya Swaminathan</b> was ICMR Director General from 2015 to 2017 and later became Deputy Director General (Programmes) of the WHO.<br>• The ICMR runs the <b>National Institute of Virology, Pune</b>, which played a key role in testing during the COVID-19 pandemic.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – डॉ. राजीव बहल</b><br><b>डॉ. राजीव बहल</b> को <b>सितंबर 2022</b> में <b>ICMR का महानिदेशक</b> तथा स्वास्थ्य अनुसंधान विभाग का सचिव नियुक्त किया गया। इससे पूर्व वे <b>विश्व स्वास्थ्य संगठन</b> में टीकाकरण व बाल स्वास्थ्य पर कार्य कर चुके हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>ICMR</b> की स्थापना <b>1911</b> में भारतीय अनुसंधान निधि संघ के रूप में हुई और <b>1949</b> में इसका नाम भारतीय आयुर्विज्ञान अनुसंधान परिषद रखा गया; मुख्यालय <b>नई दिल्ली</b> में है।<br>• यह भारत में <b>जैव-चिकित्सा अनुसंधान</b> के निर्माण, समन्वय व संवर्धन हेतु शीर्ष निकाय है और स्वास्थ्य एवं परिवार कल्याण मंत्रालय के अधीन कार्य करता है।<br>• <b>डॉ. सौम्या स्वामीनाथन</b> 2015 से 2017 तक ICMR की महानिदेशक थीं और बाद में WHO की उप महानिदेशक (कार्यक्रम) बनीं।<br>• ICMR का <b>राष्ट्रीय विषाणु विज्ञान संस्थान, पुणे</b> कोविड-19 महामारी में परीक्षण हेतु महत्वपूर्ण भूमिका निभाने वाला संस्थान है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000073917","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Who among the following is known as the 'Wizard of hockey'? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से किसे 'हॉकी का जादूगर' कहा जाता है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Dhanraj Pillay","hi":"धनराज पिल्लै"},"2":{"en":"Balbir Singh","hi":"बलबीर सिंह"},"3":{"en":"Dhyan Chand","hi":"ध्यानचंद"},"4":{"en":"Leslie Claudius","hi":"लेस्ली क्लॉडियस"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Dhyan Chand</b><br><b>Major Dhyan Chand</b> is known as the <b>Wizard of Hockey</b> for his extraordinary stickwork and goal-scoring. He won <b>three Olympic gold medals</b> in hockey, in <b>1928, 1932 and 1936</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>National Sports Day</b> is observed on <b>29 August</b>, his birthday, and the country's highest sporting honour is named the <b>Major Dhyan Chand Khel Ratna Award</b>.<br>• In the <b>1936 Berlin Olympics final</b> he scored four goals against Germany, and he scored over <b>400 goals</b> in international matches.<br>• <b>Dhanraj Pillay</b> is a former Indian hockey captain, <b>Balbir Singh</b> was a member of three Olympic gold medal teams and <b>Leslie Claudius</b> won four Olympic hockey medals.<br>• India won <b>eight Olympic gold medals</b> in hockey, a record in the sport.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – ध्यानचंद</b><br><b>मेजर ध्यानचंद</b> अपनी असाधारण स्टिक-वर्क तथा गोल करने की क्षमता के कारण <b>हॉकी का जादूगर</b> कहलाते हैं। उन्होंने <b>1928, 1932 व 1936</b> में हॉकी के <b>तीन ओलंपिक स्वर्ण</b> जीते।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उनके जन्मदिन <b>29 अगस्त</b> को <b>राष्ट्रीय खेल दिवस</b> मनाया जाता है, तथा देश का सर्वोच्च खेल सम्मान <b>मेजर ध्यानचंद खेल रत्न पुरस्कार</b> कहलाता है।<br>• <b>1936 के बर्लिन ओलंपिक फाइनल</b> में उन्होंने जर्मनी के विरुद्ध चार गोल किए, और अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मैचों में उन्होंने <b>400 से अधिक गोल</b> किए।<br>• <b>धनराज पिल्लै</b> भारतीय हॉकी टीम के पूर्व कप्तान हैं, <b>बलबीर सिंह</b> तीन ओलंपिक स्वर्ण पदक विजेता टीमों के सदस्य रहे तथा <b>लेस्ली क्लॉडियस</b> ने चार ओलंपिक पदक जीते।<br>• भारत ने हॉकी में <b>आठ ओलंपिक स्वर्ण</b> जीते हैं, जो इस खेल में एक कीर्तिमान है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000073918","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Which one of the following industries uses limestone as a principal raw material? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा उद्योग प्रमुख कच्चे माल के रूप में चूना पत्थर का उपयोग करता है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Aluminium","hi":"एल्युमिनियम"},"2":{"en":"Cement","hi":"सीमेंट"},"3":{"en":"Fertiliser","hi":"उर्वरक"},"4":{"en":"Ferromanganese","hi":"फेरोमैंगनीज़"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Cement</b><br>The <b>cement industry</b> uses <b>limestone</b> as its principal raw material, which provides the calcium oxide needed for cement. Limestone forms about <b>60 to 65 per cent</b> of the raw mix, along with clay, shale and gypsum.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The other raw materials of cement are <b>clay, shale, bauxite, iron ore and gypsum</b>, with gypsum added to control the setting time.<br>• The <b>aluminium industry</b> uses <b>bauxite</b> as its chief ore, the <b>ferromanganese</b> industry uses manganese ore and iron, and fertilisers use rock phosphate, potash and natural gas.<br>• India's cement industry is located near limestone deposits in <b>Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh, Andhra Pradesh, Telangana and Chhattisgarh</b>.<br>• Limestone is also used in the manufacture of steel, glass, paper and sugar, but cement is its largest consumer.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सीमेंट</b><br><b>सीमेंट उद्योग</b> अपने प्रमुख कच्चे माल के रूप में <b>चूना पत्थर</b> का उपयोग करता है, जो सीमेंट हेतु आवश्यक कैल्शियम ऑक्साइड देता है। कच्चे मिश्रण में चूना पत्थर लगभग <b>60 से 65 प्रतिशत</b> होता है, साथ में मिट्टी, शेल तथा जिप्सम।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सीमेंट के अन्य कच्चे माल <b>मिट्टी, शेल, बॉक्साइट, लौह अयस्क तथा जिप्सम</b> हैं; जिप्सम जमने का समय नियंत्रित करने हेतु मिलाया जाता है।<br>• <b>एल्युमिनियम उद्योग</b> का मुख्य अयस्क <b>बॉक्साइट</b> है, <b>फेरोमैंगनीज़</b> उद्योग मैंगनीज़ अयस्क व लोहा तथा उर्वरक उद्योग रॉक फॉस्फेट, पोटाश व प्राकृतिक गैस का उपयोग करता है।<br>• भारत का सीमेंट उद्योग <b>राजस्थान, मध्य प्रदेश, आंध्र प्रदेश, तेलंगाना तथा छत्तीसगढ़</b> की चूना पत्थर खदानों के निकट स्थित है।<br>• चूना पत्थर इस्पात, काँच, कागज व चीनी तथा रसायन उद्योग में भी प्रयुक्त होता है, परंतु सीमेंट इसका सबसे बड़ा उपभोक्ता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000073919","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In artistic gymnastics, which of the following apparatus is used only in men's events at the international level? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कलात्मक जिमनास्टिक में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा उपकरण अंतर्राष्ट्रीय स्तर पर केवल पुरुष स्पर्धाओं में प्रयुक्त होता है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Balance Beam","hi":"बैलेंस बीम"},"2":{"en":"Uneven Bars","hi":"अनईवन बार"},"3":{"en":"Rings","hi":"रिंग्स"},"4":{"en":"Floor","hi":"फ्लोर"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Rings</b><br>In artistic gymnastics, the <b>rings (still rings)</b> are used <b>only in men's events</b>. Women compete on the vault, uneven bars, balance beam and floor exercise, while men compete on the floor, pommel horse, rings, vault, parallel bars and horizontal bar.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>balance beam</b> and the <b>uneven bars</b> are <b>women-only</b> apparatus, and the <b>pommel horse</b>, <b>rings</b> and <b>horizontal bar</b> are men-only.<br>• The <b>floor exercise</b> and <b>vault</b> are common to both men and women.<br>• The rings are suspended about <b>2.8 metres</b> above the floor and require great upper-body strength for the cross and swing elements.<br>• Artistic gymnastics is governed by the <b>International Gymnastics Federation (FIG)</b>, founded in 1881, and India's best-known gymnast is <b>Dipa Karmakar</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – रिंग्स</b><br>कलात्मक जिमनास्टिक में <b>रिंग्स (स्टिल रिंग्स)</b> का प्रयोग <b>केवल पुरुष स्पर्धाओं</b> में होता है। महिलाएँ वॉल्ट, अनईवन बार, बैलेंस बीम व फ्लोर पर तथा पुरुष फ्लोर, पॉमेल हॉर्स, रिंग्स, वॉल्ट, पैरेलल बार व हॉरिज़ॉन्टल बार पर प्रतिस्पर्धा करते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>बैलेंस बीम</b> तथा <b>अनईवन बार</b> केवल महिलाओं के उपकरण हैं, जबकि <b>पॉमेल हॉर्स</b>, <b>रिंग्स</b> व <b>हॉरिज़ॉन्टल बार</b> केवल पुरुषों के।<br>• <b>फ्लोर एक्सरसाइज़</b> तथा <b>वॉल्ट</b> पुरुष व महिला दोनों के लिए समान हैं।<br>• रिंग्स फर्श से लगभग <b>2.8 मीटर</b> ऊपर लटकी होती हैं और क्रॉस व स्विंग तत्वों हेतु अत्यधिक शारीरिक बल चाहिए।<br>• कलात्मक जिमनास्टिक का नियामक <b>अंतर्राष्ट्रीय जिमनास्टिक महासंघ (FIG)</b> है, जिसकी स्थापना 1881 में हुई; भारत की प्रसिद्ध जिमनास्ट <b>दीपा करमाकर</b> हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000073920","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: MoUs and Agreements","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements regarding India-Nepal cooperation on transboundary rivers:<br>1) India and Nepal have jointly established the Pancheshwar Development Authority (PDA) to execute the Mahakali Treaty provisions on the Sarda River.<br>2) The Flood Forecasting &amp; Early Warning System between India and Nepal is updated quarterly during monsoon seasons.<br>Which of the above is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सीमा-पार नदियों पर भारत-नेपाल सहयोग के संबंध में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1) शारदा नदी पर महाकाली संधि के प्रावधानों के क्रियान्वयन हेतु भारत व नेपाल ने संयुक्त रूप से पंचेश्वर विकास प्राधिकरण (PDA) की स्थापना की है।<br>2) भारत व नेपाल के बीच बाढ़ पूर्वानुमान एवं चेतावनी प्रणाली मानसून के मौसम में त्रैमासिक रूप से अद्यतन की जाती है।<br>उपर्युक्त में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"Only 2","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"1 and 2 both are correct","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों सही हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2 is correct","hi":"न तो 1, न ही 2 सही है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Only 1</b><br>Statement 1 is correct: the <b>Pancheshwar Development Authority (PDA)</b> was set up jointly by India and Nepal to implement the <b>Mahakali Treaty of 1996</b>, which provides for the integrated development of the <b>Mahakali (Sarda) river</b> basin including the Pancheshwar dam.<br>Statement 2 is wrong, because the <b>Flood Forecasting and Early Warning System</b> data between the two countries is shared <b>daily</b>, not quarterly, during the monsoon.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Mahakali Treaty</b> was signed in <b>February 1996</b> and covers the Sarada Barrage, the Tanakpur Barrage and the Pancheshwar multipurpose project.<br>• The PDA has its headquarters at <b>Kathmandu</b> and its co-chairpersons are the water resources secretaries of both countries.<br>• Under the bilateral arrangement, Nepal transmits daily <b>water level and rainfall data</b> of its river sites during the monsoon to India for flood forecasting.<br>• Other India-Nepal water treaties are the <b>Kosi Agreement (1954)</b> and the <b>Gandak Agreement (1959)</b>, both revised in 1966.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केवल 1</b><br>कथन 1 सही है: <b>पंचेश्वर विकास प्राधिकरण (PDA)</b> भारत व नेपाल ने संयुक्त रूप से <b>1996 की महाकाली संधि</b> के क्रियान्वयन हेतु स्थापित किया, जो पंचेश्वर बाँध सहित <b>महाकाली (शारदा) नदी</b> बेसिन के समेकित विकास हेतु है।<br>कथन 2 गलत है, क्योंकि दोनों देशों के बीच <b>बाढ़ पूर्वानुमान एवं चेतावनी प्रणाली</b> का आँकड़ा मानसून के दौरान <b>प्रतिदिन</b> साझा किया जाता है, त्रैमासिक नहीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>महाकाली संधि</b> <b>फरवरी 1996</b> में हस्ताक्षरित हुई और इसमें सरदा बैराज, टनकपुर बैराज तथा पंचेश्वर बहुउद्देशीय परियोजना सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• PDA का मुख्यालय <b>काठमांडू</b> में है तथा इसके सह-अध्यक्ष दोनों देशों के जल संसाधन सचिव होते हैं।<br>• द्विपक्षीय व्यवस्था के अंतर्गत नेपाल मानसून के दौरान अपने नदी स्थलों का <b>जलस्तर व वर्षा आँकड़ा</b> प्रतिदिन भारत को भेजता है।<br>• भारत-नेपाल की अन्य जल संधियाँ <b>कोसी समझौता (1954)</b> तथा <b>गंडक समझौता (1959)</b> हैं, जिन्हें 1966 में संशोधित किया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000073921","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Awards and Honours","question":{"en":"Which Indian author won the <b>2022</b> International Booker Prize for 'Tomb of Sand'? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>2022</b> में 'टॉम्ब ऑफ सैंड' हेतु अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर पुरस्कार किस भारतीय लेखक ने जीता? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Arundhati Roy","hi":"अरुंधति रॉय"},"2":{"en":"Krishna Sobti","hi":"कृष्णा सोबती"},"3":{"en":"Geetanjali Shree","hi":"गीतांजलि श्री"},"4":{"en":"Kiran Desai","hi":"किरण देसाई"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Geetanjali Shree</b><br><b>Geetanjali Shree</b> won the <b>International Booker Prize 2022</b> for her novel <b>Tomb of Sand</b>, translated from Hindi <b>Ret Samadhi</b> by <b>Daisy Rockwell</b>. It was the first book translated from an Indian language to win the prize.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The International Booker Prize is given every year for a book <b>translated into English</b>, and the prize money is shared equally between the author and the translator.<br>• <b>Arundhati Roy</b> won the Booker Prize in <b>1997</b> for <b>The God of Small Things</b>, and <b>Kiran Desai</b> won it in <b>2006</b> for <b>The Inheritance of Loss</b>.<br>• <b>Krishna Sobti</b> was a major Hindi novelist who won the Jnanpith Award in 2017 for works including <b>Mitro Marjani</b>.<br>• Geetanjali Shree's other works include <b>Mai</b>, <b>Hamara Shahar Us Baras</b> and <b>Khali Jagah</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – गीतांजलि श्री</b><br><b>गीतांजलि श्री</b> ने अपने उपन्यास <b>टॉम्ब ऑफ सैंड</b> हेतु <b>2022 का अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर पुरस्कार</b> जीता, जिसका हिंदी <b>रेत समाधि</b> से <b>डेज़ी रॉकवेल</b> ने अनुवाद किया। यह पुरस्कार जीतने वाली किसी भारतीय भाषा से अनूदित पहली पुस्तक थी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर पुरस्कार प्रतिवर्ष <b>अंग्रेजी में अनूदित</b> पुस्तक को दिया जाता है, तथा पुरस्कार राशि लेखक व अनुवादक में समान रूप से बाँटी जाती है।<br>• <b>अरुंधति रॉय</b> ने <b>1997</b> में <b>द गॉड ऑफ स्मॉल थिंग्स</b> हेतु तथा <b>किरण देसाई</b> ने <b>2006</b> में <b>द इनहेरिटेंस ऑफ लॉस</b> हेतु बुकर पुरस्कार जीता।<br>• <b>कृष्णा सोबती</b> प्रमुख हिंदी उपन्यासकार थीं, जिन्हें 2017 में उनकी रचनाओं, जिनमें <b>मित्रो मरजानी</b> सम्मिलित है, हेतु ज्ञानपीठ पुरस्कार मिला।<br>• गीतांजलि श्री की अन्य रचनाएँ <b>माई</b>, <b>हमारा शहर उस बरस</b> तथा <b>खाली जगह</b> हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000073922","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"Which statement best reflects the methodology and global scope of the <b>2024</b> Corruption Perceptions Index (CPI)? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा कथन <b>2024</b> के भ्रष्टाचार अवधारणा सूचकांक (CPI) की कार्यप्रणाली तथा वैश्विक दायरे को सर्वोत्तम रूप से दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The CPI ranks countries based on actual criminal convictions","hi":"CPI देशों को वास्तविक आपराधिक दोषसिद्धियों के आधार पर रैंक करता है"},"2":{"en":"The index includes only developed countries","hi":"यह सूचकांक केवल विकसित देशों को सम्मिलित करता है"},"3":{"en":"The CPI scores are based on perceived public sector corruption and range from 0 (highly corrupt) to 100 (very clean)","hi":"CPI अंक सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र में अनुभूत भ्रष्टाचार पर आधारित होते हैं और 0 (अत्यधिक भ्रष्ट) से 100 (अत्यधिक स्वच्छ) तक होते हैं"},"4":{"en":"It ranks nations based on private sector ethical practices","hi":"यह राष्ट्रों को निजी क्षेत्र की नैतिक प्रथाओं के आधार पर रैंक करता है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – The CPI scores are based on perceived public sector corruption and range from 0 (highly corrupt) to 100 (very clean)</b><br>The <b>Corruption Perceptions Index</b> measures the <b>perceived level of corruption in the public sector</b> of countries and scores them from <b>0 (highly corrupt) to 100 (very clean)</b>, using expert assessments and opinion surveys.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The CPI is published by <b>Transparency International</b>, a Berlin-based non-governmental organisation, and is based on several independent sources of governance and expert data.<br>• In the <b>2024 CPI</b> about <b>180 countries and territories</b> were ranked; Denmark topped the index and India was placed around the 96th rank with a score of 38.<br>• The index measures <b>perceptions</b>, not actual convictions, and covers the public sector only, so options 1 and 4 are wrong.<br>• Transparency International also publishes the <b>Global Corruption Barometer</b> and the <b>Bribe Payers Index</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – CPI अंक सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र में अनुभूत भ्रष्टाचार पर आधारित होते हैं और 0 (अत्यधिक भ्रष्ट) से 100 (अत्यधिक स्वच्छ) तक होते हैं</b><br><b>भ्रष्टाचार अवधारणा सूचकांक</b> देशों के <b>सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र में भ्रष्टाचार के अनुभव किए गए स्तर</b> को मापता है और उन्हें <b>0 (अत्यधिक भ्रष्ट) से 100 (अत्यधिक स्वच्छ)</b> तक अंक देता है, जिसमें विशेषज्ञ आकलन व राय सर्वेक्षण प्रयुक्त होते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• CPI <b>ट्रांसपेरेंसी इंटरनेशनल</b> द्वारा प्रकाशित होता है, जो बर्लिन स्थित गैर-सरकारी संस्था है, तथा यह शासन व विशेषज्ञ आँकड़ों के कई स्वतंत्र स्रोतों पर आधारित है।<br>• <b>2024 के CPI</b> में लगभग <b>180 देश व क्षेत्र</b> सम्मिलित थे; डेनमार्क शीर्ष पर रहा तथा भारत 38 अंक के साथ लगभग 96वें स्थान पर रहा।<br>• यह सूचकांक <b>अनुभूति</b> मापता है, वास्तविक दोषसिद्धियाँ नहीं, तथा केवल सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र को सम्मिलित करता है, इसलिए विकल्प 1 व 4 गलत हैं।<br>• ट्रांसपेरेंसी इंटरनेशनल <b>वैश्विक भ्रष्टाचार बैरोमीटर</b> तथा <b>रिश्वत देने वालों का सूचकांक</b> भी प्रकाशित करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000073923","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Parliament","question":{"en":"What is the maximum number of members nominated by the President to the Rajya Sabha according to Article 80 of the Indian Constitution? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 80 के अनुसार राष्ट्रपति द्वारा राज्यसभा में नामित सदस्यों की अधिकतम संख्या कितनी है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ten members of the Council","hi":"परिषद के दस सदस्य"},"2":{"en":"Twelve members of the Council","hi":"परिषद के बारह सदस्य"},"3":{"en":"Fourteen members of the Council","hi":"परिषद के चौदह सदस्य"},"4":{"en":"Fifteen members of the Council","hi":"परिषद के पंद्रह सदस्य"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Twelve members of the Council</b><br>Under <b>Article 80(1)(a)</b>, the President nominates <b>twelve members</b> to the Rajya Sabha from among persons having special knowledge or practical experience in <b>literature, science, art and social service</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Rajya Sabha has a maximum strength of <b>250</b> - up to 238 representatives of states and union territories and 12 nominated members.<br>• The nominated members have <b>no right to vote in the election of the President or the Vice-President</b>, but they can vote on the removal of a Vice-President.<br>• The Rajya Sabha is a <b>permanent House</b> that is never dissolved, with one-third of its members retiring every two years under Article 83.<br>• The <b>Deputy Chairman</b> of the Rajya Sabha is elected by the House itself, unlike the Chairman, who is the Vice-President of India.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – परिषद के बारह सदस्य</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 80(1)(a)</b> के अंतर्गत राष्ट्रपति <b>बारह सदस्यों</b> को राज्यसभा में नामित करते हैं, जिनके पास <b>साहित्य, विज्ञान, कला तथा समाज सेवा</b> का विशेष ज्ञान या अनुभव होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• राज्यसभा की अधिकतम सदस्य संख्या <b>250</b> है - राज्यों व केंद्रशासित प्रदेशों के 238 प्रतिनिधि तथा 12 नामित सदस्य।<br>• नामित सदस्यों को <b>राष्ट्रपति या उपराष्ट्रपति के निर्वाचन में मतदान का अधिकार नहीं</b> होता, परंतु वे उपराष्ट्रपति को हटाने के प्रस्ताव में मतदान कर सकते हैं।<br>• राज्यसभा <b>स्थायी सदन</b> है, जिसका विघटन नहीं होता; अनुच्छेद 83 के अनुसार प्रत्येक दो वर्ष में एक-तिहाई सदस्य सेवानिवृत्त होते हैं।<br>• राज्यसभा का <b>उपसभापति</b> सदन स्वयं चुनता है, जबकि सभापति भारत के उपराष्ट्रपति होते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000073924","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Parliament","question":{"en":"As per Article 83(2), what is the normal duration of the House of the People (Lok Sabha) from the date of its first meeting? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"अनुच्छेद 83(2) के अनुसार, लोकसभा की सामान्य अवधि उसकी प्रथम बैठक की तिथि से कितनी होती है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Four years from its first meeting","hi":"इसकी प्रथम बैठक से चार वर्ष"},"2":{"en":"Five years from its first meeting","hi":"इसकी प्रथम बैठक से पाँच वर्ष"},"3":{"en":"Six years from its first meeting","hi":"इसकी प्रथम बैठक से छह वर्ष"},"4":{"en":"It is a permanent body of Parliament","hi":"यह संसद का स्थायी अंग है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Five years from its first meeting</b><br>Under <b>Article 83(2)</b>, the <b>Lok Sabha</b> continues for <b>five years from the date of its first meeting</b> and then stands dissolved, unless it is dissolved earlier. During a <b>national emergency</b>, Parliament may extend its term by one year at a time.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Rajya Sabha, under <b>Article 83(1)</b>, is a <b>permanent House</b> that is never dissolved, with one-third of its members retiring every two years.<br>• The term of the Lok Sabha was <b>six years</b> before the <b>44th Amendment Act, 1978</b>, which reduced it to five years.<br>• The <b>President may dissolve</b> the Lok Sabha under Article 85 before the end of its term on the advice of the Council of Ministers.<br>• The Lok Sabha has a maximum strength of <b>552</b> members, and it is the House to which the Council of Ministers is responsible under Article 75.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – इसकी प्रथम बैठक से पाँच वर्ष</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 83(2)</b> के अंतर्गत <b>लोकसभा</b> अपनी <b>प्रथम बैठक की तिथि से पाँच वर्ष</b> तक चलती है और उसके बाद विघटित हो जाती है, जब तक कि उसे पहले विघटित न किया जाए। <b>राष्ट्रीय आपातकाल</b> में संसद उसका कार्यकाल एक वर्ष के लिए बढ़ा सकती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 83(1)</b> के अनुसार राज्यसभा <b>स्थायी सदन</b> है जिसका विघटन नहीं होता तथा प्रत्येक दो वर्ष में एक-तिहाई सदस्य सेवानिवृत्त होते हैं।<br>• <b>44वें संशोधन अधिनियम, 1978</b> से पहले लोकसभा का कार्यकाल <b>छह वर्ष</b> था, जिसे पाँच वर्ष किया गया।<br>• <b>राष्ट्रपति</b> अनुच्छेद 85 के अंतर्गत मंत्रिपरिषद की सलाह पर लोकसभा को कार्यकाल समाप्त होने से पहले विघटित कर सकते हैं।<br>• लोकसभा की अधिकतम सदस्य संख्या <b>552</b> है, और अनुच्छेद 75 के अनुसार मंत्रिपरिषद इसी सदन के प्रति उत्तरदायी होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000073925","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Solar System","question":{"en":"What is the approximate distance between the Earth and the Sun during 'Perihelion'? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"'उपसौर (Perihelion)' के समय पृथ्वी व सूर्य के बीच की अनुमानित दूरी कितनी होती है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"147 million kilometers","hi":"147 मिलियन किलोमीटर"},"2":{"en":"142 million kilometers","hi":"142 मिलियन किलोमीटर"},"3":{"en":"152 million kilometers","hi":"152 मिलियन किलोमीटर"},"4":{"en":"160 million kilometers","hi":"160 मिलियन किलोमीटर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 147 million kilometers</b><br><b>Perihelion</b> is the point in the Earth's orbit when it is <b>closest to the Sun</b>, at a distance of about <b>147 million kilometres</b>. It occurs around <b>3 January</b> each year.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Aphelion</b> is the farthest point, at about <b>152 million kilometres</b>, and occurs around <b>4 July</b>.<br>• The average Earth-Sun distance is about <b>149.6 million kilometres</b>, which is defined as one <b>astronomical unit (AU)</b>.<br>• Because of the ellipticity of the orbit, the Earth receives about <b>7 per cent more solar radiation</b> at perihelion than at aphelion, but seasons are caused by the <b>tilt of the Earth's axis</b>, not by distance.<br>• The Earth moves fastest in its orbit at perihelion, in accordance with <b>Kepler's second law</b> of equal areas.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – 147 मिलियन किलोमीटर</b><br><b>उपसौर</b> पृथ्वी की कक्षा का वह बिंदु है जब वह <b>सूर्य के सर्वाधिक निकट</b> होती है, जो दूरी लगभग <b>147 मिलियन किलोमीटर</b> होती है। यह प्रतिवर्ष लगभग <b>3 जनवरी</b> को होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अपसौर</b> सर्वाधिक दूरी का बिंदु है, जो लगभग <b>152 मिलियन किलोमीटर</b> है और लगभग <b>4 जुलाई</b> को होता है।<br>• पृथ्वी व सूर्य की औसत दूरी लगभग <b>149.6 मिलियन किलोमीटर</b> है, जिसे एक <b>खगोलीय इकाई (AU)</b> कहा जाता है।<br>• कक्षा की दीर्घवृत्तीयता के कारण उपसौर पर पृथ्वी को अपसौर की तुलना में लगभग <b>7 प्रतिशत अधिक सौर विकिरण</b> मिलता है, परंतु ऋतुएँ <b>पृथ्वी के अक्ष के झुकाव</b> से होती हैं, दूरी से नहीं।<br>• <b>केप्लर के द्वितीय नियम</b> के अनुसार उपसौर पर पृथ्वी अपनी कक्षा में सर्वाधिक तेज चलती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000073926","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"Regarding the Earth's mantle dynamics, which statement <b>correctly</b> describes the nature of seismic wave propagation? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"पृथ्वी के मेंटल गतिकी के संबंध में कौन-सा कथन भूकंपीय तरंगों के संचरण की प्रकृति का <b>सही</b> वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"S-waves cannot traverse the liquid outer core.","hi":"S-तरंगें द्रव बाह्य क्रोड से गुजर नहीं सकतीं।"},"2":{"en":"P-waves accelerate rapidly through the Earth's mantle.","hi":"P-तरंगें पृथ्वी के मेंटल में तेजी से त्वरित होती हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Rayleigh waves travel faster than all body waves.","hi":"रेले तरंगें सभी बॉडी तरंगों से तेज चलती हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Seismic waves maintain constant velocity in mantle.","hi":"भूकंपीय तरंगें मेंटल में स्थिर वेग बनाए रखती हैं।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – S-waves cannot traverse the liquid outer core.</b><br><b>S-waves (secondary or shear waves)</b> are transverse waves that cannot pass through a <b>liquid</b>, because liquids have no shear strength. Their absence beyond a depth of about <b>2,900 km</b> proved that the <b>outer core is liquid</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>P-waves</b> are longitudinal and travel through solids, liquids and gases; they are the fastest body waves and reach a seismograph first.<br>• The <b>shadow zone</b> for S-waves between <b>105 and 142 degrees</b> from the epicentre is created by the liquid outer core blocking them.<br>• <b>Surface waves</b> such as <b>Love and Rayleigh waves</b> travel more slowly than body waves but cause the greatest damage.<br>• Seismic velocity generally <b>increases with depth</b> in the mantle but drops sharply at the core-mantle boundary, so velocity is not constant.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – S-तरंगें द्रव बाह्य क्रोड से गुजर नहीं सकतीं।</b><br><b>S-तरंगें (द्वितीयक या अपरूपण तरंगें)</b> अनुप्रस्थ तरंगें हैं, जो <b>द्रव</b> से नहीं गुजर सकतीं, क्योंकि द्रवों में अपरूपण सामर्थ्य नहीं होती। लगभग <b>2,900 किमी</b> गहराई के बाद इनकी अनुपस्थिति ने सिद्ध किया कि <b>बाह्य क्रोड द्रव है</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>P-तरंगें</b> अनुदैर्घ्य हैं और ठोस, द्रव व गैस तीनों में चलती हैं; ये सबसे तेज बॉडी तरंगें हैं और भूकंपमापी तक सबसे पहले पहुँचती हैं।<br>• S-तरंगों का <b>छाया क्षेत्र</b> अधिकेंद्र से <b>105 से 142 डिग्री</b> के बीच द्रव बाह्य क्रोड के कारण बनता है।<br>• <b>लव व रेले तरंगें</b> जैसी सतही तरंगें बॉडी तरंगों से धीमी होती हैं, परंतु सर्वाधिक विनाश करती हैं।<br>• मेंटल में भूकंपीय वेग सामान्यतः <b>गहराई के साथ बढ़ता</b> है, परंतु क्रोड-मेंटल सीमा पर तेजी से घटता है, अतः वेग स्थिर नहीं है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000073927","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Post-Gupta Dynasties","question":{"en":"Which group of monuments at Mamallapuram was carved from individual masses of rock and is an example of monolithic architecture? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"महाबलीपुरम में स्मारकों का कौन-सा समूह चट्टान के अलग-अलग खंडों से तराशा गया है और एकाश्म (मोनोलिथिक) स्थापत्य का उदाहरण है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Shore Temple","hi":"तटीय मंदिर"},"2":{"en":"Pancha Rathas","hi":"पंच रथ"},"3":{"en":"Brihadishvara Temple","hi":"बृहदीश्वर मंदिर"},"4":{"en":"Sun Temple at Konark","hi":"कोणार्क का सूर्य मंदिर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Pancha Rathas</b><br>The <b>Pancha Rathas</b> at <b>Mamallapuram</b> are five <b>monolithic</b> temples, each carved out of a <b>single large boulder</b>, built during the reign of the Pallava king <b>Narasimhavarman I (Mamalla)</b> in the 7th century.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The five rathas are named after the Pandavas - <b>Dharmaraja, Bhima, Arjuna, Nakula-Sahadeva</b> - and <b>Draupadi</b>, and they show the early evolution of Dravidian temple forms.<br>• The <b>Shore Temple</b> at Mamallapuram is built of dressed stone blocks, not a monolith, and is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.<br>• The <b>Brihadishvara Temple</b> at Thanjavur was built by <b>Rajaraja Chola I</b>, and the <b>Sun Temple at Konark</b> by <b>Narasimhadeva I</b> of the Eastern Ganga dynasty.<br>• The Mamallapuram group of monuments, including the rathas, mandapas and the Descent of the Ganges relief, is a <b>UNESCO World Heritage Site</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पंच रथ</b><br><b>महाबलीपुरम</b> के <b>पंच रथ</b> पाँच <b>एकाश्म</b> मंदिर हैं, जिनमें प्रत्येक को <b>एक बड़ी चट्टान</b> से तराशा गया। ये 7वीं शताब्दी में पल्लव राजा <b>नरसिंहवर्मन प्रथम (मामल्ल)</b> के शासनकाल में बने।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पाँच रथों का नाम पांडवों - <b>धर्मराज, भीम, अर्जुन, नकुल-सहदेव</b> - तथा <b>द्रौपदी</b> पर हैं, और ये द्रविड़ मंदिर शैली के प्रारंभिक विकास को दर्शाते हैं।<br>• महाबलीपुरम का <b>तटीय मंदिर</b> तराशे हुए पत्थर के खंडों से बना है, एकाश्म नहीं, और यह यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल है।<br>• <b>बृहदीश्वर मंदिर</b> तंजावुर में <b>राजराज चोल प्रथम</b> ने तथा <b>कोणार्क का सूर्य मंदिर</b> पूर्वी गंग वंश के <b>नरसिंहदेव प्रथम</b> ने बनवाया।<br>• रथ, मंडप तथा गंगा-अवतरण भित्ति सहित महाबलीपुरम स्मारक समूह <b>यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000073928","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: International Organisations","question":{"en":"Which international organisation, established in <b>1995</b> as the successor to the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade (GATT), regulates global trade rules? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>1995</b> में प्रशुल्क एवं व्यापार पर सामान्य समझौते (GATT) के उत्तराधिकारी के रूप में स्थापित कौन-सा अंतर्राष्ट्रीय संगठन वैश्विक व्यापार नियमों का नियमन करता है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"International Monetary Fund","hi":"अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मुद्रा कोष"},"2":{"en":"United Nations Conference on Trade and Development","hi":"संयुक्त राष्ट्र व्यापार एवं विकास सम्मेलन"},"3":{"en":"World Trade Organization","hi":"विश्व व्यापार संगठन"},"4":{"en":"Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development","hi":"आर्थिक सहयोग एवं विकास संगठन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – World Trade Organization</b><br>The <b>World Trade Organization (WTO)</b> was established on <b>1 January 1995</b> as the successor to the <b>GATT</b> and is the body that regulates <b>global trade rules</b> between member countries.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The WTO was created by the <b>Marrakesh Agreement</b> of 1994 at the conclusion of the <b>Uruguay Round</b> of trade negotiations, and its headquarters is at <b>Geneva</b>.<br>• GATT, signed in <b>1948</b>, was a treaty without a formal organisation; the WTO gave it a <b>legal and institutional</b> base.<br>• The WTO operates by <b>consensus</b>, settles disputes through its Dispute Settlement Body and has about <b>166 members</b>, with India a founding member.<br>• The <b>IMF</b> and the <b>OECD</b> deal with monetary stability and economic policy cooperation, not trade rules, and <b>UNCTAD</b> works on trade and development issues.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – विश्व व्यापार संगठन</b><br><b>विश्व व्यापार संगठन (WTO)</b> की स्थापना <b>1 जनवरी 1995</b> को <b>GATT</b> के उत्तराधिकारी के रूप में हुई और यह सदस्य देशों के बीच <b>वैश्विक व्यापार नियमों</b> का नियमन करने वाला निकाय है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• WTO की स्थापना व्यापार वार्ताओं के <b>उरुग्वे दौर</b> की समाप्ति पर <b>1994 के माराकेश समझौते</b> से हुई; इसका मुख्यालय <b>जेनेवा</b> में है।<br>• <b>1948</b> में हस्ताक्षरित GATT एक संधि थी, संगठन नहीं; WTO ने उसे <b>कानूनी व संस्थागत</b> आधार दिया।<br>• WTO <b>सर्वसम्मति</b> से कार्य करता है, विवाद निपटान निकाय के माध्यम से विवाद सुलझाता है और इसमें लगभग <b>166 सदस्य</b> हैं; भारत संस्थापक सदस्य है।<br>• <b>IMF</b> व <b>OECD</b> मौद्रिक स्थिरता तथा आर्थिक नीति सहयोग से संबंधित हैं, व्यापार नियमों से नहीं, तथा <b>UNCTAD</b> व्यापार व विकास विषयों पर कार्य करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000073929","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Magnetic Effect of Electric Current","question":{"en":"The magnetic flux through a single-turn conducting loop changes uniformly from 8 Wb (weber) to 2 Wb (weber) in 0.5 s (second). What is the magnitude of the average induced emf (electromotive force) in the loop? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एकल फेरे वाले चालक लूप से गुजरने वाला चुंबकीय फ्लक्स 0.5 सेकंड में एकसमान रूप से 8 वेबर से 2 वेबर हो जाता है। लूप में प्रेरित औसत विद्युतवाहक बल (emf) का परिमाण क्या है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3 (Volt)","hi":"3 (वोल्ट)"},"2":{"en":"6 (Volt)","hi":"6 (वोल्ट)"},"3":{"en":"12 (Volt)","hi":"12 (वोल्ट)"},"4":{"en":"18 (Volt)","hi":"18 (वोल्ट)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 12 (Volt)</b><br>By <b>Faraday's law of electromagnetic induction</b> the average induced emf is \\(e = N\\frac{\\Delta\\phi}{\\Delta t}\\). Here \\(N = 1\\), \\(\\Delta\\phi = 8 - 2 = 6\\) Wb and \\(\\Delta t = 0.5\\) s, so \\(e = \\frac{6}{0.5} = 12\\) V.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The direction of the induced current is given by <b>Lenz's law</b>, which says the induced emf opposes the change in flux that produced it.<br>• The <b>unit of magnetic flux</b> is the weber, where 1 Wb = 1 volt-second, and the unit of magnetic flux density is the tesla, where 1 T = 1 Wb per square metre.<br>• For a coil of \\(N\\) turns the induced emf is \\(N\\) times the value for one turn, so the same change in 10 turns would give 120 V.<br>• Faraday's law is the working principle of <b>generators, transformers and induction cooktops</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 12 (वोल्ट)</b><br><b>विद्युतचुंबकीय प्रेरण हेतु फैराडे के नियम</b> से औसत प्रेरित विद्युतवाहक बल \\(e = N\\frac{\\Delta\\phi}{\\Delta t}\\) होता है। यहाँ \\(N = 1\\), \\(\\Delta\\phi = 8 - 2 = 6\\) वेबर तथा \\(\\Delta t = 0.5\\) सेकंड है, अतः \\(e = \\frac{6}{0.5} = 12\\) वोल्ट।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रेरित धारा की दिशा <b>लेंज के नियम</b> से मिलती है, जिसके अनुसार प्रेरित विद्युतवाहक बल उस फ्लक्स-परिवर्तन का विरोध करता है जिससे वह उत्पन्न हुआ।<br>• <b>चुंबकीय फ्लक्स</b> की इकाई वेबर है, जहाँ 1 वेबर = 1 वोल्ट-सेकंड, तथा चुंबकीय फ्लक्स घनत्व की इकाई टेस्ला है, जहाँ 1 टेस्ला = 1 वेबर प्रति वर्ग मीटर।<br>• \\(N\\) फेरों वाली कुंडली का प्रेरित विद्युतवाहक बल एक फेरे से \\(N\\) गुना होता है, अतः 10 फेरों में उतना ही परिवर्तन 120 वोल्ट देगा।<br>• फैराडे का नियम <b>जनित्र, ट्रांसफार्मर व इंडक्शन चूल्हों</b> का कार्य सिद्धांत है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000073930","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Cell","question":{"en":"A bacterial culture initially contains 200 bacteria and doubles in size every hour. How many bacteria will be present after 3 hours? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी जीवाणु कल्चर में प्रारंभ में 200 जीवाणु हैं और यह प्रत्येक घंटे में दोगुना हो जाता है। 3 घंटे बाद कितने जीवाणु होंगे? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"400"},"2":{"en":"800"},"3":{"en":"1200"},"4":{"en":"1600"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – 1600</b><br>The population doubles every hour, so after \\(n\\) hours the number is \\(200 \\times 2^{n}\\). For \\(n = 3\\), the count is \\(200 \\times 2^{3} = 200 \\times 8 = 1600\\) bacteria.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Step by step: after 1 hour 400, after 2 hours 800 and after 3 hours <b>1600</b> bacteria.<br>• Such growth is called <b>exponential growth</b> and is described by \\(N = N_0 \\times 2^{t/g}\\), where \\(g\\) is the generation time.<br>• Bacteria reproduce mainly by <b>binary fission</b>, an asexual method in which one cell divides into two identical daughter cells.<br>• In bacteria the genetic material is not enclosed in a nucleus, so they are <b>prokaryotes</b>, and their growth curve has lag, log, stationary and decline phases.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – 1600</b><br>जनसंख्या प्रत्येक घंटे दोगुनी होती है, अतः \\(n\\) घंटे बाद संख्या \\(200 \\times 2^{n}\\) होती है। \\(n = 3\\) हेतु यह \\(200 \\times 2^{3} = 200 \\times 8 = 1600\\) जीवाणु होगी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• चरणबद्ध रूप से: 1 घंटे बाद 400, 2 घंटे बाद 800 तथा 3 घंटे बाद <b>1600</b> जीवाणु।<br>• ऐसी वृद्धि <b>चरघातांकी वृद्धि</b> कहलाती है और इसे \\(N = N_0 \\times 2^{t/g}\\) से व्यक्त किया जाता है, जहाँ \\(g\\) जनन काल है।<br>• जीवाणु मुख्यतः <b>द्विखंडन</b> से प्रजनन करते हैं, जिसमें एक कोशिका दो समान संतति कोशिकाओं में बँटती है।<br>• जीवाणुओं में आनुवंशिक पदार्थ केंद्रक में परिबद्ध नहीं होता, इसलिए वे <b>प्रोकैरियोट</b> हैं; उनकी वृद्धि वक्र में लैग, लॉग, स्थिर तथा क्षय चरण होते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000073931","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A solid metallic sphere is converted into a wire of radius 0.2 cm and length 240 m. What was the radius of the sphere? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"धातु के एक ठोस गोले को 0.2 cm त्रिज्या और 240 m लंबाई वाले तार में बदला जाता है। गोले की त्रिज्या क्या थी? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8.96 cm"},"2":{"en":"2.54 cm"},"3":{"en":"6.28 cm"},"4":{"en":"5.45 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"135\" height=\"125\" viewBox=\"0 0 135 125\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"50\"/><path d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M65 65H115\"/><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"61\">R</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">0.2</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">24000</text></g></svg><br>Length = 240 m = 24000 cm<br>Volume of sphere = volume of wire<br>\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi R^3 = \\pi (0.2)^2 \\times 24000 = 960\\pi\\)<br>\\(R^3 = 720 \\Rightarrow R = \\sqrt[3]{720} \\approx \\boxed{8.96}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 8.96 cm.</b><br><br><b>Note:</b> The SSC paper printed this option as 8.94 cm (approximate); it has been corrected to 8.96 cm.","hi":"<svg width=\"135\" height=\"125\" viewBox=\"0 0 135 125\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"50\"/><path d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M65 65H115\"/><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"61\">R</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">0.2</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">24000</text></g></svg><br>लंबाई = 240 m = 24000 cm<br>गोले का आयतन = तार का आयतन<br>\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi R^3 = \\pi (0.2)^2 \\times 24000 = 960\\pi\\)<br>\\(R^3 = 720 \\Rightarrow R = \\sqrt[3]{720} \\approx \\boxed{8.96}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 8.96 cm है।</b><br><br><b>नोट:</b> SSC प्रश्नपत्र में यह विकल्प 8.94 cm (लगभग) छपा था; इसे सुधारकर 8.96 cm किया गया है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000073932","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If sinA = 3/5, and A is acute, find the value of sin²A + cos²A + tan²A. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि sinA = 3/5 है, और A न्यून कोण है, तो sin²A + cos²A + tan²A का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"25/16"},"4":{"en":"5"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sin^2 A + \\cos^2 A = 1\\)<br>\\(\\sin A = \\frac{3}{5} \\Rightarrow \\cos A = \\frac{4}{5},\\ \\tan A = \\frac{3}{4}\\)<br>Value = \\(1 + \\frac{9}{16} = \\boxed{\\frac{25}{16}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 25/16.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sin^2 A + \\cos^2 A = 1\\)<br>\\(\\sin A = \\frac{3}{5} \\Rightarrow \\cos A = \\frac{4}{5},\\ \\tan A = \\frac{3}{4}\\)<br>मान = \\(1 + \\frac{9}{16} = \\boxed{\\frac{25}{16}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 25/16 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000073933","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The ratio of the volumes of two cones is 2:3, and the ratio of the radii of their bases is 4:5. What is the ratio of their heights? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो शंकुओं के आयतनों का अनुपात 2:3 है, और उनके आधारों की त्रिज्याओं का अनुपात 4:5 है। उनकी ऊँचाइयों का अनुपात क्या है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25 : 24"},"2":{"en":"19 : 16"},"3":{"en":"16 : 25"},"4":{"en":"17 : 18"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M70 15L20 110M70 15L120 110M20 110a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 110a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 15V110M70 110H120\"/><path d=\"M70 100h8v10\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"106\">4k</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"72\">h₁</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\"></text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"170\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M70 15L20 110M70 15L120 110M20 110a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 110a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 15V110M70 110H120\"/><path d=\"M70 100h8v10\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"106\">5k</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"72\">h₂</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\"></text></g></svg><br>V ∝ r²h → \\(\\frac{h_1}{h_2} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} \\times \\frac{r_2^2}{r_1^2}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{2}{3} \\times \\frac{25}{16} = \\frac{25}{24}\\)<br>\\(h_1 : h_2 = \\boxed{25 : 24}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 25 : 24.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M70 15L20 110M70 15L120 110M20 110a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 110a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 15V110M70 110H120\"/><path d=\"M70 100h8v10\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"106\">4k</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"72\">h₁</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\"></text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"170\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M70 15L20 110M70 15L120 110M20 110a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 110a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 15V110M70 110H120\"/><path d=\"M70 100h8v10\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"106\">5k</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"72\">h₂</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\"></text></g></svg><br>V ∝ r²h → \\(\\frac{h_1}{h_2} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} \\times \\frac{r_2^2}{r_1^2}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{2}{3} \\times \\frac{25}{16} = \\frac{25}{24}\\)<br>\\(h_1 : h_2 = \\boxed{25 : 24}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 25 : 24 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000073934","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"If the radius of a cone is reduced by 20% while the height remains the same, by what percentage does its volume decrease? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि एक शंकु की त्रिज्या 20% कम कर दी जाए जबकि ऊँचाई समान रहे, तो इसके आयतन में कितने प्रतिशत की कमी होती है? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20%"},"2":{"en":"36%"},"3":{"en":"40%"},"4":{"en":"48%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M70 15L20 110M70 15L120 110M20 110a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 110a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 15V110M70 110H120\"/><path d=\"M70 100h8v10\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"106\">r</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"72\">h</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\">l</text></g></svg><br>V ∝ r² (h constant)<br>New volume = \\((0.8)^2 = 0.64\\) times<br>Decrease = \\(\\boxed{36\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 36%.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M70 15L20 110M70 15L120 110M20 110a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 110a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 15V110M70 110H120\"/><path d=\"M70 100h8v10\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"106\">r</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"72\">h</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\">l</text></g></svg><br>V ∝ r² (h स्थिर)<br>नया आयतन = \\((0.8)^2 = 0.64\\) गुना<br>कमी = \\(\\boxed{36\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 36% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000073935","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"If \\(\\frac{(1.6)^3 - K}{(1.6)^2 + 0.8 + 0.25} = 1.1\\), find the value of \\(K\\). [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\frac{(1.6)^3 - K}{(1.6)^2 + 0.8 + 0.25} = 1.1\\) है, तो \\(K\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1.345"},"2":{"en":"0.125"},"3":{"en":"0.565"},"4":{"en":"1.785"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Denominator = \\(a^2 + ab + b^2\\) with a = 1.6, b = 0.5 (ab = 0.8, b² = 0.25)<br>\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b = 1.1\\) ✔ → K = \\(b^3\\)<br>\\(K = (0.5)^3 = \\boxed{0.125}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 0.125.</b>","hi":"हर = \\(a^2 + ab + b^2\\), जहाँ a = 1.6, b = 0.5 (ab = 0.8, b² = 0.25)<br>\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b = 1.1\\) ✔ → K = \\(b^3\\)<br>\\(K = (0.5)^3 = \\boxed{0.125}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 0.125 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000073936","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A can complete a certain work in 20 days, while B can complete the same work in 30 days. Both start working together and continue for 6 days, after which A stops working. How many more days will B need to complete the remaining work on his own? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A किसी कार्य को 20 दिनों में पूरा कर सकता है, जबकि B उसी कार्य को 30 दिनों में पूरा कर सकता है। दोनों एक साथ कार्य शुरू करते हैं और 6 दिनों तक करते हैं, जिसके बाद A कार्य करना बंद कर देता है। शेष कार्य को अकेले पूरा करने के लिए B को और कितने दिन लगेंगे? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12 days","hi":"12 दिन"},"2":{"en":"15 days","hi":"15 दिन"},"3":{"en":"18 days","hi":"18 दिन"},"4":{"en":"24 days","hi":"24 दिन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Work = LCM(20, 30) = 60 units → A = 3/day, B = 2/day<br>6 days together: \\(5 \\times 6 = 30\\) units<br>Remaining 30 units by B = \\(\\frac{30}{2} = \\boxed{15}\\) days<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 15 days.</b>","hi":"कार्य = LCM(20, 30) = 60 इकाई → A = 3/दिन, B = 2/दिन<br>6 दिन साथ में: \\(5 \\times 6 = 30\\) इकाई<br>शेष 30 इकाई B द्वारा = \\(\\frac{30}{2} = \\boxed{15}\\) दिन<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 15 दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000073937","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"Riya and Supriti have two glasses of equal volume. Both have some milk in their glasses. Riya says to Supriti, “Give me half of the milk in your glass so that my glass will be full of milk.” Supriti says to Riya, “Instead, you give me one-fourth of the milk in your glass so that my glass will be full of milk.” Find the ratio of volumes of milk in their glasses. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"रिया और सुप्रीति के पास समान आयतन के दो गिलास हैं। दोनों के गिलास में कुछ दूध है। रिया सुप्रीति से कहती है, “अपने गिलास का आधा दूध मुझे दे दो ताकि मेरा गिलास दूध से भर जाए।” सुप्रीति रिया से कहती है, “इसके बजाय, तुम अपने गिलास का एक-चौथाई दूध मुझे दे दो ताकि मेरा गिलास दूध से भर जाए।” उनके गिलासों में दूध के आयतनों का अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1:3"},"2":{"en":"3:4"},"3":{"en":"2:3"},"4":{"en":"1:2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Riya = r, Supriti = s, glass = V<br>\\(r + \\frac{s}{2} = V\\) and \\(s + \\frac{r}{4} = V\\)<br>\\(r + \\frac{s}{2} = s + \\frac{r}{4} \\Rightarrow \\frac{3r}{4} = \\frac{s}{2}\\)<br>\\(r : s = \\boxed{2 : 3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 2:3.</b>","hi":"रिया = r, सुप्रीति = s, गिलास = V<br>\\(r + \\frac{s}{2} = V\\) और \\(s + \\frac{r}{4} = V\\)<br>\\(r + \\frac{s}{2} = s + \\frac{r}{4} \\Rightarrow \\frac{3r}{4} = \\frac{s}{2}\\)<br>\\(r : s = \\boxed{2 : 3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 2:3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000073938","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"Partnership between A and B is such that A invests ₹2,500 more than B. B’s investment period is 6 months, whereas A’s is 10 months. Out of the total profit of ₹5,300, A’s profit share comes to ₹3,500. What was B’s investment? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A और B के बीच साझेदारी इस प्रकार है कि A, B से ₹2,500 अधिक निवेश करता है। B की निवेश अवधि 6 महीने है, जबकि A की 10 महीने है। ₹5,300 के कुल लाभ में से A का हिस्सा ₹3,500 आता है। B का निवेश कितना था? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹18,000"},"2":{"en":"₹15,000"},"3":{"en":"₹24,000"},"4":{"en":"₹20,000"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A : B profit = 3500 : 1800 = 35 : 18<br>\\(\\frac{10(x + 2500)}{6x} = \\frac{35}{18} \\Rightarrow 180(x + 2500) = 210x\\)<br>\\(30x = 450000 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{15000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹15,000.</b>","hi":"A : B लाभ = 3500 : 1800 = 35 : 18<br>\\(\\frac{10(x + 2500)}{6x} = \\frac{35}{18} \\Rightarrow 180(x + 2500) = 210x\\)<br>\\(30x = 450000 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{15000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹15,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000073939","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"Rohit spends 25% of his annual income on groceries, 30% on rent, and 20% on miscellaneous expenses. If his yearly savings are ₹75,600, find his annual income. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"रोहित अपनी वार्षिक आय का 25% किराने पर, 30% किराए पर और 20% विविध खर्चों पर व्यय करता है। यदि उसकी वार्षिक बचत ₹75,600 है, तो उसकी वार्षिक आय ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹2,52,800"},"2":{"en":"₹1,24,000"},"3":{"en":"₹3,02,400"},"4":{"en":"₹4,30,600"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Savings = 100% − (25% + 30% + 20%) = 25%<br>25% = 75600<br>Income = \\(75600 \\times 4 = \\boxed{302400}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹3,02,400.</b>","hi":"बचत = 100% − (25% + 30% + 20%) = 25%<br>25% = 75600<br>आय = \\(75600 \\times 4 = \\boxed{302400}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹3,02,400 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000073940","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A sum of money amounts to ₹9,440 in 3 years and to ₹10,400 in 5 years at a certain rate of simple interest. If the interest rate increases by 2%, in how many years will the original principal double? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"साधारण ब्याज की एक निश्चित दर पर एक धनराशि 3 वर्षों में ₹9,440 और 5 वर्षों में ₹10,400 हो जाती है। यदि ब्याज दर 2% बढ़ जाए, तो मूल मूलधन कितने वर्षों में दोगुना हो जाएगा? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10 years 4 months","hi":"10 वर्ष 4 महीने"},"2":{"en":"12 years 8 months","hi":"12 वर्ष 8 महीने"},"3":{"en":"12 years 6 months","hi":"12 वर्ष 6 महीने"},"4":{"en":"10 years 2 months","hi":"10 वर्ष 2 महीने"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"SI for 2 years = 10400 − 9440 = 960 → 480 per year<br>P = 9440 − 3 × 480 = 8000 → rate = \\(\\frac{480}{8000} \\times 100 = 6\\%\\)<br>New rate = 8%; doubling needs SI = 100% → time = \\(\\frac{100}{8} = 12.5\\) years<br>\\(= \\boxed{12 \\text{ years } 6 \\text{ months}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12 years 6 months.</b>","hi":"2 वर्षों का साधारण ब्याज = 10400 − 9440 = 960 → 480 प्रति वर्ष<br>P = 9440 − 3 × 480 = 8000 → दर = \\(\\frac{480}{8000} \\times 100 = 6\\%\\)<br>नई दर = 8%; दोगुना होने के लिए ब्याज = 100% → समय = \\(\\frac{100}{8} = 12.5\\) वर्ष<br>\\(= \\boxed{12 \\text{ years } 6 \\text{ months}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12 वर्ष 6 महीने है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000073941","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"An equilateral triangle is inscribed in a circle of radius 6 cm. Find the area of the triangle. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"6 cm त्रिज्या वाले एक वृत्त में एक समबाहु त्रिभुज अंकित है। त्रिभुज का क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(27\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²"},"2":{"en":"\\(27\\sqrt{7}\\) cm²"},"3":{"en":"\\(21\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²"},"4":{"en":"\\(21\\sqrt{7}\\) cm²"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"155\" height=\"160\" viewBox=\"0 0 155 160\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"80\" r=\"60\"/><path d=\"M75 20L23 110L127 110Z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M75 80L127 110\"/><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"80\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"75\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"17\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"end\">B</text><text x=\"133\" y=\"122\">C</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"end\">O</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"91\">6</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"125\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a</text></g></svg><br>Side \\(a = R\\sqrt{3} = 6\\sqrt{3}\\) cm<br>Area = \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} a^2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times 108\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{27\\sqrt{3}}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(27\\sqrt{3}\\) cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"155\" height=\"160\" viewBox=\"0 0 155 160\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"80\" r=\"60\"/><path d=\"M75 20L23 110L127 110Z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M75 80L127 110\"/><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"80\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"75\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"17\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"end\">B</text><text x=\"133\" y=\"122\">C</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"end\">O</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"91\">6</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"125\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a</text></g></svg><br>भुजा \\(a = R\\sqrt{3} = 6\\sqrt{3}\\) cm<br>क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} a^2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times 108\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{27\\sqrt{3}}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(27\\sqrt{3}\\) cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000073942","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A wheel of diameter 1.4 m makes 250 revolutions. Find the distance travelled (in meters). (Take \\(\\pi = \\frac{22}{7}\\)) [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1.4 m व्यास वाला एक पहिया 250 चक्कर लगाता है। तय की गई दूरी (मीटर में) ज्ञात कीजिए। (\\(\\pi = \\frac{22}{7}\\) लीजिए) [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1100 m"},"2":{"en":"900 m"},"3":{"en":"1200 m"},"4":{"en":"600 m"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"130\" height=\"130\" viewBox=\"0 0 130 130\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"50\"/><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M65 65H115\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"60\">0.7</text></g></svg><br>One revolution = \\(\\pi d = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 1.4 = 4.4\\) m<br>250 revolutions = \\(4.4 \\times 250 = \\boxed{1100}\\) m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1100 m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"130\" height=\"130\" viewBox=\"0 0 130 130\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"50\"/><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M65 65H115\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"60\">0.7</text></g></svg><br>एक चक्कर = \\(\\pi d = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 1.4 = 4.4\\) m<br>250 चक्कर = \\(4.4 \\times 250 = \\boxed{1100}\\) m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1100 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000073943","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"Two wristwatches were sold for ₹1,980 each. One was sold at a 10% profit and the other at a 10% loss. What was the total loss in the transaction? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो कलाई घड़ियाँ ₹1,980 प्रत्येक में बेची गईं। एक 10% लाभ पर और दूसरी 10% हानि पर बेची गई। इस सौदे में कुल हानि कितनी थी? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹20"},"2":{"en":"₹40"},"3":{"en":"₹60"},"4":{"en":"₹80"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"CP₁ = \\(\\frac{1980}{1.1} = 1800\\), CP₂ = \\(\\frac{1980}{0.9} = 2200\\) → total CP = 4000<br>Total SP = 3960<br>Loss = 4000 − 3960 = \\(\\boxed{40}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹40.</b>","hi":"क्रय मूल्य₁ = \\(\\frac{1980}{1.1} = 1800\\), क्रय मूल्य₂ = \\(\\frac{1980}{0.9} = 2200\\) → कुल क्रय मूल्य = 4000<br>कुल विक्रय मूल्य = 3960<br>हानि = 4000 − 3960 = \\(\\boxed{40}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹40 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000073944","section":"MATH","topic":"Discount","question":{"en":"A shopkeeper allows a 20% discount on the marked price. What should be the marked price of an article costing ₹4000 to earn 25% profit? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक दुकानदार अंकित मूल्य पर 20% छूट देता है। ₹4000 क्रय मूल्य वाली वस्तु पर 25% लाभ कमाने के लिए उसका अंकित मूल्य क्या होना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹6250"},"2":{"en":"₹4990"},"3":{"en":"₹7400"},"4":{"en":"₹5870"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"SP = \\(4000 \\times 1.25 = 5000\\)<br>SP = 80% of MP<br>MP = \\(\\frac{5000}{0.8} = \\boxed{6250}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ₹6250.</b>","hi":"विक्रय मूल्य = \\(4000 \\times 1.25 = 5000\\)<br>विक्रय मूल्य = अंकित मूल्य का 80%<br>अंकित मूल्य = \\(\\frac{5000}{0.8} = \\boxed{6250}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ₹6250 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000073945","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\tan\\theta = 2\\), find the value of \\(\\frac{\\sec^2\\theta - \\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta}{\\sec^2\\theta + \\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta}\\). [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\tan\\theta = 2\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{\\sec^2\\theta - \\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta}{\\sec^2\\theta + \\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{5}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2}{5}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(-\\frac{3}{5}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(-\\frac{2}{5}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sec^2\\theta = 1 + 4 = 5,\\ \\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta = 1 + \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{5}{4}\\)<br>Value = \\(\\frac{5 - \\frac{5}{4}}{5 + \\frac{5}{4}} = \\frac{15/4}{25/4}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{3}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{3}{5}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\sec^2\\theta = 1 + 4 = 5,\\ \\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta = 1 + \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{5}{4}\\)<br>मान = \\(\\frac{5 - \\frac{5}{4}}{5 + \\frac{5}{4}} = \\frac{15/4}{25/4}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{3}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{3}{5}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000073946","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sqrt{5} = 2.236\\), then find the value of \\(\\frac{10 - \\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}\\). [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sqrt{5} = 2.236\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{10 - \\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1.452"},"2":{"en":"3.472"},"3":{"en":"4.587"},"4":{"en":"5.256"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{10 - \\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5}} - 1 = 2\\sqrt{5} - 1\\)<br>\\(= 4.472 - 1 = \\boxed{3.472}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 3.472.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{10 - \\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5}} - 1 = 2\\sqrt{5} - 1\\)<br>\\(= 4.472 - 1 = \\boxed{3.472}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 3.472 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000073947","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = \\sqrt{5}\\), then find the value of \\(x^2 - \\frac{1}{x^2}\\). [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = \\sqrt{5}\\) है, तो \\(x^2 - \\frac{1}{x^2}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\pm\\sqrt{5}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\pm\\sqrt{7}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\pm\\sqrt{8}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\pm\\sqrt{3}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 = 5 - 4 = 1 \\Rightarrow x - \\frac{1}{x} = \\pm 1\\)<br>\\(x^2 - \\frac{1}{x^2} = \\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{5} \\times (\\pm 1) = \\boxed{\\pm\\sqrt{5}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\pm\\sqrt{5}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 = 5 - 4 = 1 \\Rightarrow x - \\frac{1}{x} = \\pm 1\\)<br>\\(x^2 - \\frac{1}{x^2} = \\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{5} \\times (\\pm 1) = \\boxed{\\pm\\sqrt{5}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\pm\\sqrt{5}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000073948","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"An exterior angle of a regular polygon is 36°. What is the total number of diagonals that can be drawn in this polygon? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक सम बहुभुज का बाह्य कोण 36° है। इस बहुभुज में कुल कितने विकर्ण खींचे जा सकते हैं? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"21"},"2":{"en":"18"},"3":{"en":"39"},"4":{"en":"35"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"n = \\(\\frac{360^\\circ}{36^\\circ} = 10\\)<br>Diagonals = \\(\\frac{n(n - 3)}{2} = \\frac{10 \\times 7}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{35}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 35.</b>","hi":"n = \\(\\frac{360^\\circ}{36^\\circ} = 10\\)<br>विकर्ण = \\(\\frac{n(n - 3)}{2} = \\frac{10 \\times 7}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{35}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 35 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000073949","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In triangle △ABC, points D and E lie on sides AC and BC, respectively, such that DE is parallel to AB. A point F is located on segment CE, and DF is parallel to AE. If CE = 6 cm and CF = 2.5 cm, find the length of BC. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"त्रिभुज △ABC में, बिंदु D और E क्रमशः भुजाओं AC और BC पर इस प्रकार स्थित हैं कि DE, AB के समांतर है। एक बिंदु F रेखाखंड CE पर स्थित है, और DF, AE के समांतर है। यदि CE = 6 cm और CF = 2.5 cm है, तो BC की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"13.8 cm"},"2":{"en":"17 cm"},"3":{"en":"14.4 cm"},"4":{"en":"18 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"270\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 270 185\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M120 15L30 165H230ZM82 78L166 78M30 165L166 78M82 78L139 41\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">C</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"169\">A</text><text x=\"234\" y=\"169\">B</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"82\">D</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"82\">E</text><text x=\"144\" y=\"43\">F</text><text x=\"157\" y=\"56\">CE = 6</text><text x=\"138\" y=\"26\">2.5</text></g></svg><br>In ΔCAE, DF ∥ AE → \\(\\frac{CF}{CE} = \\frac{CD}{CA}\\)<br>In ΔCAB, DE ∥ AB → \\(\\frac{CE}{CB} = \\frac{CD}{CA}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{CF}{CE} = \\frac{CE}{CB} \\Rightarrow CB = \\frac{CE^2}{CF} = \\frac{36}{2.5}\\)<br>BC = \\(\\boxed{14.4}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 14.4 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"270\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 270 185\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M120 15L30 165H230ZM82 78L166 78M30 165L166 78M82 78L139 41\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">C</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"169\">A</text><text x=\"234\" y=\"169\">B</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"82\">D</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"82\">E</text><text x=\"144\" y=\"43\">F</text><text x=\"157\" y=\"56\">CE = 6</text><text x=\"138\" y=\"26\">2.5</text></g></svg><br>ΔCAE में, DF ∥ AE → \\(\\frac{CF}{CE} = \\frac{CD}{CA}\\)<br>ΔCAB में, DE ∥ AB → \\(\\frac{CE}{CB} = \\frac{CD}{CA}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{CF}{CE} = \\frac{CE}{CB} \\Rightarrow CB = \\frac{CE^2}{CF} = \\frac{36}{2.5}\\)<br>BC = \\(\\boxed{14.4}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 14.4 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000073950","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A circle has diameter 58 cm. Two equal chords PQ and RS are parallel. PS is a diameter. If PQ is 20 cm from the centre, find the length of RS. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक वृत्त का व्यास 58 cm है। दो बराबर जीवाएँ PQ और RS समांतर हैं। PS एक व्यास है। यदि PQ केंद्र से 20 cm दूर है, तो RS की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"28 cm"},"2":{"en":"42 cm"},"3":{"en":"56 cm"},"4":{"en":"84 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"185\" height=\"170\" viewBox=\"0 0 185 170\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"85\" r=\"65\"/><path d=\"M43 40H137M43 130H137M43 40L137 130\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M90 85V40M90 85L137 40\"/><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"85\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"39\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"end\">P</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"38\">Q</text><text x=\"39\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"end\">R</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"140\">S</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"89\" text-anchor=\"end\">O</text><text x=\"86\" y=\"67\" text-anchor=\"end\">20</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"69\">29</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"36\" text-anchor=\"middle\">21</text></g></svg><br>Radius = 29 cm; half of PQ = \\(\\sqrt{29^2 - 20^2} = \\sqrt{441} = 21\\) cm<br>PQ = 42 cm; RS = PQ (equal chords)<br>RS = \\(\\boxed{42}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 42 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"185\" height=\"170\" viewBox=\"0 0 185 170\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"85\" r=\"65\"/><path d=\"M43 40H137M43 130H137M43 40L137 130\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M90 85V40M90 85L137 40\"/><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"85\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"39\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"end\">P</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"38\">Q</text><text x=\"39\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"end\">R</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"140\">S</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"89\" text-anchor=\"end\">O</text><text x=\"86\" y=\"67\" text-anchor=\"end\">20</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"69\">29</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"36\" text-anchor=\"middle\">21</text></g></svg><br>त्रिज्या = 29 cm; PQ का आधा = \\(\\sqrt{29^2 - 20^2} = \\sqrt{441} = 21\\) cm<br>PQ = 42 cm; RS = PQ (बराबर जीवाएँ)<br>RS = \\(\\boxed{42}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 42 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000073951","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Tangents PA and PB are drawn to a circle with center O from point P outside the circle. If the angle between the tangents \\(\\angle APB = 60^\\circ\\) and the radius OA = 10 cm, find the length of the chord AB. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वृत्त के बाहर स्थित बिंदु P से केंद्र O वाले एक वृत्त पर स्पर्श रेखाएँ PA और PB खींची जाती हैं। यदि स्पर्श रेखाओं के बीच का कोण \\(\\angle APB = 60^\\circ\\) है और त्रिज्या OA = 10 cm है, तो जीवा AB की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(10\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"},"2":{"en":"12 cm"},"3":{"en":"\\(14\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"},"4":{"en":"18 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"277\" height=\"202\" viewBox=\"0 0 277 202\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M251 101L138 36M101 101L138 36M251 101L138 166M135 42L141 46L145 40M138 36L138 166M232 90A22 22 0 0 0 232 112\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M101 101L138 166M101 101L251 101\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"101\" r=\"75\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"101\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"91\" y=\"105\">O</text><text x=\"261\" y=\"105\">P</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"28\">A</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"182\">B</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"67\">10</text><text x=\"219\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\angle AOB = 180^\\circ - 60^\\circ = 120^\\circ\\)<br>AB = \\(2r\\sin\\frac{120^\\circ}{2} = 2 \\times 10 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(10\\sqrt{3}\\) cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"277\" height=\"202\" viewBox=\"0 0 277 202\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M251 101L138 36M101 101L138 36M251 101L138 166M135 42L141 46L145 40M138 36L138 166M232 90A22 22 0 0 0 232 112\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M101 101L138 166M101 101L251 101\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"101\" r=\"75\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"101\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"91\" y=\"105\">O</text><text x=\"261\" y=\"105\">P</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"28\">A</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"182\">B</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"67\">10</text><text x=\"219\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\angle AOB = 180^\\circ - 60^\\circ = 120^\\circ\\)<br>AB = \\(2r\\sin\\frac{120^\\circ}{2} = 2 \\times 10 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(10\\sqrt{3}\\) cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000073952","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A pendulum of length 75 cm swings through an angle of 24°. What is the length of the arc traced by its bob? (Use π = 3.14) [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"75 cm लंबाई वाला एक लोलक 24° के कोण से दोलन करता है। इसके गोलक द्वारा बनाए गए चाप की लंबाई क्या है? (π = 3.14 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25.6 cm"},"2":{"en":"28.4 cm"},"3":{"en":"31.4 cm"},"4":{"en":"38.6 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"130\" height=\"132\" viewBox=\"0 0 130 132\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M102 73L20 110H110A90 90 0 0 0 102 73\"/><path d=\"M38 110A18 18 0 0 0 36 103\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"65\" y=\"125\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75</text><text x=\"41\" y=\"105\">24°</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"114\">O</text></g></svg><br>Arc = \\(\\frac{24}{360} \\times 2 \\times 3.14 \\times 75\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{15} \\times 471 = \\boxed{31.4}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 31.4 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"130\" height=\"132\" viewBox=\"0 0 130 132\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M102 73L20 110H110A90 90 0 0 0 102 73\"/><path d=\"M38 110A18 18 0 0 0 36 103\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"65\" y=\"125\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75</text><text x=\"41\" y=\"105\">24°</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"114\">O</text></g></svg><br>चाप = \\(\\frac{24}{360} \\times 2 \\times 3.14 \\times 75\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{15} \\times 471 = \\boxed{31.4}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 31.4 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000073953","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two circles of different radii intersect at two points, A and B. A direct common tangent touches the circles at points P and Q. If the extension of the common chord AB meets the tangent line PQ at point X, and PX=6 cm, find the length of the segment PQ in centimeters. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भिन्न त्रिज्याओं वाले दो वृत्त दो बिंदुओं A और B पर प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं। एक सीधी उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा वृत्तों को बिंदुओं P और Q पर स्पर्श करती है। यदि उभयनिष्ठ जीवा AB का विस्तार स्पर्श रेखा PQ को बिंदु X पर मिलता है, और PX = 6 cm है, तो रेखाखंड PQ की लंबाई सेंटीमीटर में ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9 cm"},"2":{"en":"10 cm"},"3":{"en":"12 cm"},"4":{"en":"16 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"297\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"0 0 297 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M106 26L244 56M175 144L175 41\"/><circle cx=\"105\" cy=\"107\" r=\"79\"/><circle cx=\"216\" cy=\"107\" r=\"55\"/><circle cx=\"175\" cy=\"41\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"119\" y=\"27\">P</text><text x=\"231\" y=\"51\">Q</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"38\">X</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"74\">A</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"155\">B</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"33\">6</text></g></svg><br>X lies on line AB extended (common chord), so by the tangent–secant theorem for each circle:<br>\\(XP^2 = XA \\times XB = XQ^2 \\Rightarrow XP = XQ\\)<br>X is the midpoint of PQ → PQ = 2 × 6 = \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"297\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"0 0 297 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M106 26L244 56M175 144L175 41\"/><circle cx=\"105\" cy=\"107\" r=\"79\"/><circle cx=\"216\" cy=\"107\" r=\"55\"/><circle cx=\"175\" cy=\"41\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"119\" y=\"27\">P</text><text x=\"231\" y=\"51\">Q</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"38\">X</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"74\">A</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"155\">B</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"33\">6</text></g></svg><br>X, AB (उभयनिष्ठ जीवा) के विस्तार पर है, अतः प्रत्येक वृत्त के लिए स्पर्शरेखा–छेदक प्रमेय से:<br>\\(XP^2 = XA \\times XB = XQ^2 \\Rightarrow XP = XQ\\)<br>X, PQ का मध्य-बिंदु है → PQ = 2 × 6 = \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000073954","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Given that \\(m - n = 7\\) and \\(mn = 18\\), find the value of \\((m + n)^2\\). [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिया गया है कि \\(m - n = 7\\) और \\(mn = 18\\) है, तो \\((m + n)^2\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"49"},"2":{"en":"324"},"3":{"en":"72"},"4":{"en":"121"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\((m + n)^2 = (m - n)^2 + 4mn\\)<br>\\(= 49 + 72 = \\boxed{121}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 121.</b>","hi":"\\((m + n)^2 = (m - n)^2 + 4mn\\)<br>\\(= 49 + 72 = \\boxed{121}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 121 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000073955","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A tank initially contains 200 litres of a mixture of alcohol and water in the ratio 9:11. A certain volume of the mixture is removed and replaced with an equal volume of pure alcohol, making the new ratio of alcohol to water 3:2. Approximately how many litres of the mixture were replaced (rounded to two decimal places)? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक टंकी में शुरू में 200 लीटर अल्कोहल और पानी का मिश्रण 9:11 के अनुपात में है। मिश्रण की एक निश्चित मात्रा निकालकर उतनी ही मात्रा में शुद्ध अल्कोहल मिलाया जाता है, जिससे अल्कोहल और पानी का नया अनुपात 3:2 हो जाता है। लगभग कितने लीटर मिश्रण बदला गया (दो दशमलव स्थानों तक)? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"54.55 litres","hi":"54.55 लीटर"},"2":{"en":"51.25 litres","hi":"51.25 लीटर"},"3":{"en":"67.05 litres","hi":"67.05 लीटर"},"4":{"en":"35.55 litres","hi":"35.55 लीटर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Water initially = \\(\\frac{11}{20} \\times 200 = 110\\) L; finally = \\(\\frac{2}{5} \\times 200 = 80\\) L<br>Only water removed with the mixture: \\(110\\left(1 - \\frac{x}{200}\\right) = 80\\)<br>\\(\\frac{x}{200} = \\frac{3}{11} \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{600}{11} \\approx \\boxed{54.55}\\) L<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 54.55 litres.</b>","hi":"प्रारंभ में पानी = \\(\\frac{11}{20} \\times 200 = 110\\) L; अंत में = \\(\\frac{2}{5} \\times 200 = 80\\) L<br>पानी केवल निकाले गए मिश्रण के साथ घटता है: \\(110\\left(1 - \\frac{x}{200}\\right) = 80\\)<br>\\(\\frac{x}{200} = \\frac{3}{11} \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{600}{11} \\approx \\boxed{54.55}\\) L<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 54.55 लीटर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000073956","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Which of the following is incorrectly spelled? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Viceregal"},"2":{"en":"Egregious"},"3":{"en":"Magnanimity"},"4":{"en":"Opprobreum"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Opprobrium (निंदा) = public disgrace or severe criticism.</b><br><b>Opprobreum</b> is incorrectly spelled; the ending should be “-ium.”<br><b>Viceregal</b> = relating to a viceroy; <b>egregious</b> = conspicuously bad.<br><b>Magnanimity</b> = generosity of spirit; both are correctly spelled.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Opprobreum.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000073957","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correctly spelt word.<br>The team proposed a ___ solution that addressed all major concerns. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"comprihensive"},"2":{"en":"comprehansive"},"3":{"en":"comprehenzive"},"4":{"en":"comprehensive"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Comprehensive (व्यापक) = including all or nearly all aspects.</b><br>The correct spelling is “comprehensive.”<br><b>Comprihensive</b> uses “i” instead of “e”; <b>comprehansive</b> uses “a.”<br><b>Comprehenzive</b> incorrectly uses “z.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): comprehensive.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000073958","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correctly spelt word.<br>Their argument was weakened by ___ assumptions not supported by data. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"tenious"},"2":{"en":"tenuous"},"3":{"en":"tenuos"},"4":{"en":"tennuous"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Tenuous (दुर्बल) = weak, slight or insubstantial.</b><br>The correct spelling is “tenuous.”<br><b>Tenious</b> uses “i” instead of “u”; <b>tenuos</b> omits “u.”<br><b>Tennuous</b> doubles “n.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): tenuous.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000073959","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blanks with the appropriate article.<br>Although ___ emergence of artificial intelligence promises significant benefits, it also raises ___ host of ethical dilemmas. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"a, the"},"2":{"en":"the, a"},"3":{"en":"an, the"},"4":{"en":"the, the"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “The” is used for a specific thing; “a host of” is a fixed expression meaning “a large number of”.</b><br>“The emergence of artificial intelligence” refers to one particular development, so it takes “the”.<br>“A host of ethical dilemmas” is the fixed phrase; “the host of” changes the meaning to a specific host.<br>Correct sentence: Although <b>the</b> emergence of artificial intelligence promises significant benefits, it also raises <b>a</b> host of ethical dilemmas.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): the, a.</b><br><br><b>Note:</b> SSC's official answer key marked option (4): the, the as correct, which is logically incorrect. This is a <b>bonus question</b>."},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000073960","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>As global debt levels reached an all-time high,<br>P. raising concerns over potential defaults and economic downturns,<br>Q. developing nations struggled to service their loans due to rising interest rates,<br>R. while major economies implemented austerity measures to curb fiscal imbalances<br>S. prompting international financial institutions to consider restructuring debt repayment plans, [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"SRPQ"},"2":{"en":"PQSR"},"3":{"en":"RPQS"},"4":{"en":"QSPR"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QSPR</b><br>Q states how developing nations responded to rising interest rates.<br>S gives the institutional consequence of their repayment difficulty.<br>P adds concerns about defaults, and R contrasts the austerity measures of major economies.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): QSPR.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000073961","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Improve the sentence by selecting the appropriate adverb of the underlined word.<br>He <b>deeply</b> agreed to the proposal after much thought. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"immediately"},"2":{"en":"reluctantly"},"3":{"en":"suddenly"},"4":{"en":"eagerly"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Reluctantly (अनिच्छा से) = unwillingly or with hesitation.</b><br>“After much thought” suggests hesitation before agreement.<br>Correct sentence: “He <b>reluctantly</b> agreed to the proposal after much thought.”<br>The other adverbs do not fit the deliberation as naturally.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): reluctantly.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000073962","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>Recent medical trials,<br>P. previously considered untreatable<br>Q. in targeting rare genetic disorders<br>R. have yielded promising results<br>S. involving MRNA technology, [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"SRQP"},"2":{"en":"PSRQ"},"3":{"en":"QPRS"},"4":{"en":"RSPQ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: SRQP</b><br>S describes the trials as involving MRNA technology.<br>R supplies the main predicate: they have yielded promising results.<br>Q identifies their target, and P describes the disorders as previously untreatable.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): SRQP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000073963","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br>He came across with an old friend at the conference. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"friend"},"2":{"en":"came"},"3":{"en":"across with"},"4":{"en":"conference"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Come across someone” means to meet someone unexpectedly. The preposition “with” is not used in this expression.</b><br>Correct sentence: “He <b>came across</b> an old friend at the conference.”<br>The erroneous phrase is “across with.” Remove “with” to make the sentence grammatically correct.<br>“At the conference” is correctly used to indicate the location of the meeting.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): across with.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000073964","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Which of the following options is NOT one of the meanings of the homonym “tender”? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"An offer to carry out work or supply goods at a stated price"},"2":{"en":"Showing gentleness or concern"},"3":{"en":"A legal document authorizing someone to conduct a trial"},"4":{"en":"A small boat used to ferry people or supplies to a larger ship"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Tender (निविदा) = a formal offer to supply goods or perform work.</b><br><b>Tender (कोमल)</b> = gentle or caring<br><b>Tender (सहायक नौका)</b> = a small boat serving a larger vessel<br>A document authorizing a trial is not a meaning of “tender.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): A legal document authorizing someone to conduct a trial.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000073965","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The menstrual cycle, frequently distilled into reductive explanations within mainstream discourse, constitutes a complex, finely-tuned hormonal symphony that underpins female reproductive viability. Typically spanning around 28 days—though significant interindividual variability persists—the cycle is anatomically and biochemically demarcated into four sequential phases: menstruation, the follicular phase, ovulation, and the luteal phase.<br><br>Menstruation initiates with the systematic desquamation of the functional layer of the endometrium, an event precipitated by the precipitous decline in circulating levels of estrogen and progesterone following an unfertilized ovulatory event. Thereafter, during the follicular phase, anterior pituitary secretion of follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) catalyses the recruitment and maturation of ovarian follicles. A single dominant follicle subsequently prevails, secreting escalating quantities of estrogen to promote proliferative thickening of the endometrial lining in anticipation of potential zygote implantation.<br><br>Mid-cycle, ovulation ensues, triggered by an acute surge of luteinizing hormone (LH), culminating in the release of an oocyte into the fallopian tube—a transient but critical window of maximal fertility. In the absence of fertilization, the luteal phase commences: the residual follicular structure, now termed the corpus luteum, secretes progesterone to stabilize the endometrial architecture. Without embryonic implantation, corpus luteum regression ensues, hormonal concentrations diminish sharply, and the cyclical endometrial shedding recommences.<br><br>Despite the endogenous predictability of this sequence, the menstrual cycle exhibits considerable vulnerability to extrinsic perturbations—including psychosocial stressors, systemic illnesses, and environmental variables—underscoring the intricate interplay between endocrine function and broader homeostatic mechanisms.<br><br><br>Identify the correct transformation of the sentence.<br>“Menstruation initiates with the systematic desquamation of the functional layer of the endometrium.”<br>Which option correctly transforms it into a passive voice without changing the meaning? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The functional layer of the endometrium is systematically desquamated, initiating menstruation."},"2":{"en":"Menstruation is initiating by the desquamation of the functional layer."},"3":{"en":"The systematic endometrium desquamates itself to initiate menstruation."},"4":{"en":"The menstruation systematically desquamates the functional layer of the endometrium."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The object of “desquamates” becomes the passive subject.</b><br>“The functional layer … is systematically desquamated” preserves the process that initiates menstruation.<br>B uses an incorrect passive verb form; C changes the agent and structure.<br>D remains active and reverses the intended relationship.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The functional layer of the endometrium is systematically desquamated, initiating menstruation.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000073966","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The menstrual cycle, frequently distilled into reductive explanations within mainstream discourse, constitutes a complex, finely-tuned hormonal symphony that underpins female reproductive viability. Typically spanning around 28 days—though significant interindividual variability persists—the cycle is anatomically and biochemically demarcated into four sequential phases: menstruation, the follicular phase, ovulation, and the luteal phase.<br><br>Menstruation initiates with the systematic desquamation of the functional layer of the endometrium, an event precipitated by the precipitous decline in circulating levels of estrogen and progesterone following an unfertilized ovulatory event. Thereafter, during the follicular phase, anterior pituitary secretion of follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) catalyses the recruitment and maturation of ovarian follicles. A single dominant follicle subsequently prevails, secreting escalating quantities of estrogen to promote proliferative thickening of the endometrial lining in anticipation of potential zygote implantation.<br><br>Mid-cycle, ovulation ensues, triggered by an acute surge of luteinizing hormone (LH), culminating in the release of an oocyte into the fallopian tube—a transient but critical window of maximal fertility. In the absence of fertilization, the luteal phase commences: the residual follicular structure, now termed the corpus luteum, secretes progesterone to stabilize the endometrial architecture. Without embryonic implantation, corpus luteum regression ensues, hormonal concentrations diminish sharply, and the cyclical endometrial shedding recommences.<br><br>Despite the endogenous predictability of this sequence, the menstrual cycle exhibits considerable vulnerability to extrinsic perturbations—including psychosocial stressors, systemic illnesses, and environmental variables—underscoring the intricate interplay between endocrine function and broader homeostatic mechanisms.<br><br><br>What is the closest synonym for the word “precipitous” as used in the passage? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gradual"},"2":{"en":"Abrupt"},"3":{"en":"Moderate"},"4":{"en":"Predictable"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Precipitous (अचानक, तीव्र) = sudden and steep.</b><br>The passage describes a sharp hormonal decline after an unfertilized ovulatory event.<br><b>Abrupt (अचानक)</b> is the closest synonym.<br>Gradual, moderate and predictable do not express the suddenness.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Abrupt.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000073967","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The menstrual cycle, frequently distilled into reductive explanations within mainstream discourse, constitutes a complex, finely-tuned hormonal symphony that underpins female reproductive viability. Typically spanning around 28 days—though significant interindividual variability persists—the cycle is anatomically and biochemically demarcated into four sequential phases: menstruation, the follicular phase, ovulation, and the luteal phase.<br><br>Menstruation initiates with the systematic desquamation of the functional layer of the endometrium, an event precipitated by the precipitous decline in circulating levels of estrogen and progesterone following an unfertilized ovulatory event. Thereafter, during the follicular phase, anterior pituitary secretion of follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) catalyses the recruitment and maturation of ovarian follicles. A single dominant follicle subsequently prevails, secreting escalating quantities of estrogen to promote proliferative thickening of the endometrial lining in anticipation of potential zygote implantation.<br><br>Mid-cycle, ovulation ensues, triggered by an acute surge of luteinizing hormone (LH), culminating in the release of an oocyte into the fallopian tube—a transient but critical window of maximal fertility. In the absence of fertilization, the luteal phase commences: the residual follicular structure, now termed the corpus luteum, secretes progesterone to stabilize the endometrial architecture. Without embryonic implantation, corpus luteum regression ensues, hormonal concentrations diminish sharply, and the cyclical endometrial shedding recommences.<br><br>Despite the endogenous predictability of this sequence, the menstrual cycle exhibits considerable vulnerability to extrinsic perturbations—including psychosocial stressors, systemic illnesses, and environmental variables—underscoring the intricate interplay between endocrine function and broader homeostatic mechanisms.<br><br><br>According to the passage, what is the primary function of the corpus luteum during the luteal phase? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To trigger menstruation by lowering progesterone."},"2":{"en":"To secrete hormones that maintain endometrial integrity."},"3":{"en":"To stimulate another round of follicle maturation."},"4":{"en":"To dissolve immediately after ovulation."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: The corpus luteum secretes progesterone to stabilize the endometrial architecture.</b><br>Its hormonal secretion maintains the uterine lining in anticipation of implantation.<br>It regresses only when embryonic implantation does not occur.<br>The other options contradict this passage.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): To secrete hormones that maintain endometrial integrity.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000073968","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The menstrual cycle, frequently distilled into reductive explanations within mainstream discourse, constitutes a complex, finely-tuned hormonal symphony that underpins female reproductive viability. Typically spanning around 28 days—though significant interindividual variability persists—the cycle is anatomically and biochemically demarcated into four sequential phases: menstruation, the follicular phase, ovulation, and the luteal phase.<br><br>Menstruation initiates with the systematic desquamation of the functional layer of the endometrium, an event precipitated by the precipitous decline in circulating levels of estrogen and progesterone following an unfertilized ovulatory event. Thereafter, during the follicular phase, anterior pituitary secretion of follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) catalyses the recruitment and maturation of ovarian follicles. A single dominant follicle subsequently prevails, secreting escalating quantities of estrogen to promote proliferative thickening of the endometrial lining in anticipation of potential zygote implantation.<br><br>Mid-cycle, ovulation ensues, triggered by an acute surge of luteinizing hormone (LH), culminating in the release of an oocyte into the fallopian tube—a transient but critical window of maximal fertility. In the absence of fertilization, the luteal phase commences: the residual follicular structure, now termed the corpus luteum, secretes progesterone to stabilize the endometrial architecture. Without embryonic implantation, corpus luteum regression ensues, hormonal concentrations diminish sharply, and the cyclical endometrial shedding recommences.<br><br>Despite the endogenous predictability of this sequence, the menstrual cycle exhibits considerable vulnerability to extrinsic perturbations—including psychosocial stressors, systemic illnesses, and environmental variables—underscoring the intricate interplay between endocrine function and broader homeostatic mechanisms.<br><br><br>Choose the correct form of the verb for the blank:<br>“Despite the endogenous predictability of this sequence, the menstrual cycle ___ considerable vulnerability to extrinsic perturbations.” [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"exhibits"},"2":{"en":"exhibit"},"3":{"en":"exhibiting"},"4":{"en":"exhibited"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The singular subject “the menstrual cycle” takes “exhibits.”</b><br>The passage states a general fact in simple present tense.<br>“Exhibit” lacks agreement, and “exhibiting” is non-finite.<br>“Exhibited” unnecessarily shifts the fact into the past.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): exhibits.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000073969","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>The menstrual cycle, frequently distilled into reductive explanations within mainstream discourse, constitutes a complex, finely-tuned hormonal symphony that underpins female reproductive viability. Typically spanning around 28 days—though significant interindividual variability persists—the cycle is anatomically and biochemically demarcated into four sequential phases: menstruation, the follicular phase, ovulation, and the luteal phase.<br><br>Menstruation initiates with the systematic desquamation of the functional layer of the endometrium, an event precipitated by the precipitous decline in circulating levels of estrogen and progesterone following an unfertilized ovulatory event. Thereafter, during the follicular phase, anterior pituitary secretion of follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) catalyses the recruitment and maturation of ovarian follicles. A single dominant follicle subsequently prevails, secreting escalating quantities of estrogen to promote proliferative thickening of the endometrial lining in anticipation of potential zygote implantation.<br><br>Mid-cycle, ovulation ensues, triggered by an acute surge of luteinizing hormone (LH), culminating in the release of an oocyte into the fallopian tube—a transient but critical window of maximal fertility. In the absence of fertilization, the luteal phase commences: the residual follicular structure, now termed the corpus luteum, secretes progesterone to stabilize the endometrial architecture. Without embryonic implantation, corpus luteum regression ensues, hormonal concentrations diminish sharply, and the cyclical endometrial shedding recommences.<br><br>Despite the endogenous predictability of this sequence, the menstrual cycle exhibits considerable vulnerability to extrinsic perturbations—including psychosocial stressors, systemic illnesses, and environmental variables—underscoring the intricate interplay between endocrine function and broader homeostatic mechanisms.<br><br><br>What does “desquamation” most closely mean in the context of the passage? [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Thickening of the uterine lining"},"2":{"en":"Shedding of the surface layer"},"3":{"en":"Hormone secretion"},"4":{"en":"Cell multiplication"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Desquamation (बाहरी परत का झड़ना) = shedding of an outer layer of tissue.</b><br>During menstruation, the functional endometrial layer is shed.<br>Thickening occurs during the follicular phase, not desquamation.<br>Hormone secretion and cell multiplication are different processes.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Shedding of the surface layer.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000073970","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>LAUD</b> [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ridicule"},"2":{"en":"Mockery"},"3":{"en":"Praise"},"4":{"en":"Criticism"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Laud (प्रशंसा करना) = praise highly.</b><br><b>Ridicule (उपहास)</b> = mock or deride<br><b>Mockery (मज़ाक)</b> = ridicule<br><b>Praise (प्रशंसा)</b> = express approval or admiration ✔<br><b>Criticism (आलोचना)</b> = disapproval; synonyms: acclaim, commend, extol.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Praise.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000073971","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Vituperative</b> [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Complimentary"},"2":{"en":"Abusive"},"3":{"en":"Scolding"},"4":{"en":"Vindictive"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Vituperative (गालीपूर्ण) = bitterly abusive.</b><br><b>Complimentary (प्रशंसापूर्ण)</b> = expressing praise ✔<br><b>Abusive (अपमानजनक)</b> = insulting<br><b>Scolding (डाँटने वाला)</b> = rebuking<br><b>Vindictive (प्रतिशोधी)</b> = seeking revenge; other antonyms: laudatory, approving.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Complimentary.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000073972","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom:<br>Gild the lily [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To beautify something already perfect"},"2":{"en":"To plant lilies in spring"},"3":{"en":"To decorate unnecessarily"},"4":{"en":"To misrepresent reality"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Gild the lily (आवश्यकता से अधिक सजाना) = try to improve something already beautiful.</b><br>Example: “Adding more effects would only gild the lily.”<br>Planting lilies is literal, and misrepresentation is not implied.<br>The idiom emphasizes unnecessary improvement of something already excellent.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): To beautify something already perfect.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000073973","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom:<br>The die is cast [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A new choice is offered"},"2":{"en":"An irreversible decision has been made"},"3":{"en":"There's a risk involved"},"4":{"en":"The plan has failed"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>The die is cast (निर्णय अब अटल है) = an irrevocable step has been taken.</b><br>Example: “Once the resignation was submitted, the die was cast.”<br>The idiom does not mean a new choice or mere risk.<br>It also does not imply that the plan has failed.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): An irreversible decision has been made.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000073974","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Acquiescent</b> [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Agreeable"},"2":{"en":"Obliging"},"3":{"en":"Obdurate"},"4":{"en":"Obsequious"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Acquiescent (सहमत) = ready to accept without protest.</b><br><b>Agreeable (सहमत)</b> = willing to agree<br><b>Obliging (सहायक)</b> = willing to help<br><b>Obdurate (हठी)</b> = stubbornly refusing to change ✔<br><b>Obsequious (चापलूस)</b> = excessively obedient; other antonyms: resistant, defiant.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Obdurate.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000073975","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “A person who believes that people are motivated purely by self-interest”. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Cynic"},"2":{"en":"Fatalist"},"3":{"en":"Stoic"},"4":{"en":"Epicure"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Cynic (आलोचक/संदेहवादी) = one who distrusts human sincerity and sees self-interest.</b><br><b>Fatalist (भाग्यवादी)</b> = believes events are predetermined<br><b>Stoic (स्थिरचित्त)</b> = endures pain without complaint<br><b>Epicure (स्वाद-विशेषज्ञ)</b> = enjoys fine food and drink<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Cynic.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000073976","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>Fire destroyed the warehouse last night. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The warehouse was destroyed last night."},"2":{"en":"The warehouse is destroyed last night."},"3":{"en":"The warehouse had been destroyed last night."},"4":{"en":"The warehouse has been destroyed last night."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple past passive = was/were + past participle.</b><br>The object “the warehouse” becomes the singular subject.<br>“Was destroyed” preserves the past event and time expression.<br>The other options use incorrect present, past perfect or present perfect forms.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The warehouse was destroyed last night.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000073977","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:<br>She is known to have been mentoring interns remotely throughout the year. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It is known that she has mentored interns remotely this year."},"2":{"en":"She has been mentoring interns remotely, it is known."},"3":{"en":"Interns were known to be remotely mentored by her."},"4":{"en":"She is known to mentor interns remotely during the year."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Subject + is known + to have been + V-ing” becomes “It is known / people know that + subject + has been + V-ing”.</b><br>The original keeps the present perfect continuous idea (“to have been mentoring”), so the active form must keep “has been mentoring”.<br>Option 2 keeps the same tense and meaning: “She has been mentoring interns remotely, it is known.”<br>Option 1 changes the tense to “has mentored” and “this year”; option 3 changes the subject and tense; option 4 changes the tense to “to mentor”.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): She has been mentoring interns remotely, it is known.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000073978","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:<br>The accused was understood to have been acting under pressure from influential figures. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It was understood that the accused had been acting under pressure."},"2":{"en":"The understanding was that the pressure caused the accused to act."},"3":{"en":"The accused understood to act under pressure."},"4":{"en":"Influential figures acted through the accused, as was understood."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Subject + was understood + to have been + V-ing” becomes “It was understood that + subject + had been + V-ing”.</b><br>“Was understood” (past) with “to have been acting” shifts to the past perfect continuous “had been acting”.<br>Option 1 keeps the same tense and meaning: “It was understood that the accused had been acting under pressure.”<br>Option 2 changes the meaning, option 3 drops the passive sense (“understood to act”), and option 4 says the influential figures acted, which is not stated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): It was understood that the accused had been acting under pressure.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000073979","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in direct speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding indirect speech.<br>They said, “We are watching a movie.” [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They said they are watching a movie."},"2":{"en":"They said they had watched a movie."},"3":{"en":"They said that they were watching a movie."},"4":{"en":"They said that we watched a movie."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Present continuous becomes past continuous after “said.”</b><br>“We are watching” becomes “they were watching.”<br>A retains present continuous, B changes to past perfect.<br>D retains “we” and changes the aspect.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): They said that they were watching a movie.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000073980","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a logical passage.<br>1. Therefore, critical thinking skills are increasingly valued.<br>2. In the modern information age, data is abundant.<br>3. However, discerning reliable information from misinformation is challenging.<br>4. Education systems are adapting to cultivate these abilities. [SSC CGL 15/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-1-3-4"},"2":{"en":"2-4-1-3"},"3":{"en":"3-4-2-1"},"4":{"en":"2-3-1-4"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-3-1-4</b><br>Sentence 2 introduces abundant data, and sentence 3 presents the difficulty of judging reliability.<br>Sentence 1 gives the consequence: critical thinking is valued.<br>Sentence 4 concludes with educational adaptation.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 2-3-1-4.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};